INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvicb9ue000moku87op29jga','c023a9a1-be0e-4e37-a8f7-4f8220eded1b','assistant','I''ll help you search for heart images. Let me search for heart images in your knowledge base and online medical references.

I found several excellent heart image resources for you:

**[S1] Heart Anatomy** - Texas Heart Institute
https://www.texasheart.org/heart-health/heart-information-center/topics/heart-anatomy
Your heart has 4 chambers. The upper chambers are called the left and right atria, and the lower chambers are called the left and right ventricles.

**[S2] Atlas of Human Cardiac Anatomy - University of Minnesota**
https://www.vhlab.umn.edu/atlas
The atlas of human cardiac anatomy has live videos and still images of reanimated human hearts in a variety of views. Free to download and use.

**[S3] "Human Heart Anatomy" Images – Browse 1068**
https://stock.adobe.com/search?k=%22human+heart+anatomy%22
Human heart anatomy diagram showing blood flow and vessel connections. 3D medical animation of blood circulation through human heart, lungs, and upper body.

**[S4] Heart: illustrated anatomy | e-Anatomy**
https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/thorax/heart
This interactive atlas of human heart anatomy is based on medical illustrations and cadaver photography. The user can show or hide the anatomical labels.

**[S5] Frontal View of Heart Interior Anatomy Diagram Explained**
https://www.facebook.com/abdallah89othman/videos/check-out-this-detailed-frontal-view-of-the-heart-interior-a-great-visual-for-un/1395890264963827
The animation shows the heart''s chambers, the cardiac artery, the right and left heart chambers, the cardiac vent, and the cardiac muscle.

These resources offer various types of heart images including anatomical diagrams, interactive atlases, 3D animations, and educational illustrations. The University of Minnesota atlas and e-Anatomy seem particularly comprehensive for medical study purposes.','[{"id":"call_-7145227680911192372","name":"search_medical_references","args":{"query":"heart anatomy medical images","maxResults":5}}]','[{"toolCallId":"call_-7145227680911192372","toolName":"search_medical_references","content":"{\\"results\\":[{\\"title\\":\\"Heart Anatomy\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.texasheart.org/heart-health/heart-information-center/topics/heart-anatomy\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Your heart has 4 chambers . The upper chambers are called the left and right atria, and the lower chambers are called the left and right ventricles.\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.texasheart.org\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Atlas of Human Cardiac Anatomy - University of Minnesota\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.vhlab.umn.edu/atlas\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"The atlas of human cardiac anatomy has live videos and still images of reanimated human hearts in a variety of views. free to download and use\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.vhlab.umn.edu\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"\\\\\\"Human Heart Anatomy\\\\\\" Images – Browse 1068\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://stock.adobe.com/search?k=%22human+heart+anatomy%22\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"human heart anatomy diagram showing blood flow and vessel connections . 3D medical animation of blood circulation through human heart, lungs, and upper body.\\",\\"host\\":\\"stock.adobe.com\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Heart: illustrated anatomy | e-Anatomy\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/thorax/heart\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"This interactive atlas of human heart anatomy is based on medical illustrations and cadaver photography. The user can show or hide the anatomical labels\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.imaios.com\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Frontal View of Heart Interior Anatomy Diagram Expla