INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvicelwp000toku8fdmx91a5','73bdc608-3741-4e81-8f01-c323e9d3573a','assistant','I''ll search for real medical images of the heart for you.

I found several excellent sources for real medical images of the heart:

## Key Resources for Real Heart Images:

**[S4] Atlas of Human Cardiac Anatomy - University of Minnesota**
- **URL**: https://www.vhlab.umn.edu/atlas
- This appears to be the most comprehensive resource, featuring live videos and still images of reanimated human hearts in various anatomical views
- Images are free to download and use for educational purposes

**[S3] Labeled Heart Images (University of Michigan BlueLink)**
- **URL**: https://sites.google.com/a/umich.edu/bluelink/resources/bluelink/heart
- Provides labeled heart images that can be downloaded
- Good for educational reference with clear anatomical labels

**[S2] Heart Anatomy (Texas Heart Institute)**
- **URL**: https://www.texasheart.org/heart-health/heart-information-center/topics/heart-anatomy
- Offers detailed heart anatomy information with accompanying images
- Covers the four-chamber structure (atria and ventricles)

**[S5] Heart Anatomy: Structure, Valves, Coronary Vessels (KenHub)**
- **URL**: https://www.kenhub.com/en/library/anatomy/heart
- Comprehensive heart anatomy resource with multiple images
- Focuses on structure, valves, and coronary vessels

**[S1] Real Cardiac Anatomy Research**
- **URL**: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30675928
- Academic research discussing authentic cardiac anatomy representations
- May provide insights into how real hearts differ from textbook illustrations

The University of Minnesota''s Atlas of Human Cardiac Anatomy ([S4]) is particularly valuable as it contains actual human heart specimens with multiple viewing angles and is specifically designed for medical education.','[{"id":"call_-7145228333746220358","name":"search_medical_references","args":{"query":"real medical images heart anatomy pathology","maxResults":5}}]','[{"toolCallId":"call_-7145228333746220358","toolName":"search_medical_references","content":"{\\"results\\":[{\\"title\\":\\"What is the real cardiac anatomy?\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30675928\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"by S Mori · 2019 · Cited by 166 — It is almost universal at present for textbooks of anatomy to illustrate the heart as if removed from the body and positioned on its apex, the so-called ...\\",\\"host\\":\\"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Heart Anatomy\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.texasheart.org/heart-health/heart-information-center/topics/heart-anatomy\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Your heart has 4 chambers . The upper chambers are called the left and right atria, and the lower chambers are called the left and right ventricles. Normal  ...\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.texasheart.org\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Labeled Heart Images\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://sites.google.com/a/umich.edu/bluelink/resources/bluelink/heart\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Labeled Heart Images . To download a BlueLink image, click on the photo and select the download option on the following page. Read more\\",\\"host\\":\\"sites.google.com\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Atlas of Human Cardiac Anatomy - University of Minnesota\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.vhlab.umn.edu/atlas\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"The atlas of human cardiac anatomy has live videos and still images of reanimated human hearts in a variety of views. are free to download and use\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.vhlab.umn.edu\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Heart anatomy: Structure, valves, coronary vessels\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.kenhub.com/en/library/anatomy/heart\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"This page discusses the heart anatomy . Click here to learn everything about the anatomy of the heart, heart valves and vessels at Kenhub!\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.kenhub.com\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"}],\\"formatted\\":\\"[S1] What is the real cardiac anatomy?\\\\n    https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30675928 (pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov)\\\\n    by S Mori · 2019 · Cited by 166 — It is almost universal at present for textbooks of anatomy to illustrate the heart as if removed from the body and positioned on its apex, the so-called ...\\\\n[S2] Heart Anatomy\\\\n    https://www.texasheart.org/heart-health/heart-information-center/topics/heart-anatomy (www.texasheart.org)\\\\n    Your heart has 4 chambers . The upper chambers are called the left and right atria, and the lower chambers are called the left and right ventricles. Normal  ...\\\\n[S3] Labeled Heart Images\\\\n    https://sites.google.com/a/umich.edu/bluelink/resources/bluelink/heart (sites.google.com)\\\\n    Labeled Heart Images . To download a BlueLink image, click on the photo and select the download option on the following page. Read more\\\\n[S4] Atlas of Human Cardiac Anatomy - University of Minnesota\\\\n    https://www.vhlab.umn.edu/atlas (www.vhlab.umn.edu)\\\\n    The atlas of human cardiac anatomy has live videos and still images of reanimated human hearts in a variety of views. are free to download and use\\\\n[S5] Heart anatomy: Structure, valves, coronary vessels\\\\n    https://www.kenhub.com/en/library/anatomy/heart (www.kenhub.com)\\\\n    This page discusses the heart anatomy . Click here to learn everything about the anatomy of the heart, heart valves and vessels at Kenhub!\\",\\"note\\":\\"Cite these URLs inline in your answer.\\"}","isError":false}]',NULL,'2026-10-21T16:44:50.665Z');
