INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvie3w9r0023oku82kzfi2yx','f82124c7-24e8-470e-a2c5-7fa16c6300fc','user','show me a sample lab panel for a patient with hyperkalemia',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-21T17:32:30.108Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvie46s40024oku83t5rnn99','f82124c7-24e8-470e-a2c5-7fa16c6300fc','assistant','I''ll create a sample lab panel for a patient with hyperkalemia. This will include typical findings you might see in a patient with elevated potassium levels.

Here''s a sample lab panel for a patient with hyperkalemia:

![Basic Metabolic Panel - Hyperkalemia](/generated/lab-7b247d53-0d76.svg)

**Key Lab Values:**
| Test | Result | Reference Range | Status |
|------|--------|-----------------|---------|
| Sodium | 138 mmol/L | 135-145 | Normal |
| **Potassium** | **6.8 mmol/L** | 3.5-5.0 | **High** |
| Chloride | 102 mmol/L | 98-107 | Normal |
| Bicarbonate | 18 mmol/L | 22-26 | Low |
| BUN | 42 mg/dL | 7-20 | High |
| Creatinine | 3.2 mg/dL | 0.6-1.2 | High |
| Glucose | 128 mg/dL | 70-100 | High |
| Calcium | 8.9 mg/dL | 8.5-10.5 | Normal |

This lab panel shows several key findings consistent with hyperkalemia:

1. **Elevated potassium (6.8 mmol/L)** - The primary finding, significantly above the normal range
2. **Elevated BUN and creatinine** - Indicates acute or chronic kidney disease, a common cause of hyperkalemia
3. **Metabolic acidosis (low bicarbonate)** - Often accompanies hyperkalemia due to acid-base disturbances in renal failure
4. **Mild hyperglycemia** - May be present due to stress response or underlying diabetes

This pattern is typical in a patient with chronic kidney disease (CKD) who may have reduced potassium excretion capacity. The elevated potassium could be exacerbated by medications, dietary potassium intake, or acute kidney injury.','[{"id":"call_-7145216445276746037","name":"render_lab_panel","args":{"title":"Basic Metabolic Panel - Hyperkalemia","subtitle":"Patient: 68M with CKD, Day 2 of admission","rows":[{"test":"Sodium","result":"138","units":"mmol/L","reference":"135-145","flag":""},{"test":"Potassium","result":"6.8","units":"mmol/L","reference":"3.5-5.0","flag":"H"},{"test":"Chloride","result":"102","units":"mmol/L","reference":"98-107","flag":""},{"test":"Bicarbonate","result":"18","units":"mmol/L","reference":"22-26","flag":"L"},{"test":"BUN","result":"42","units":"mg/dL","reference":"7-20","flag":"H"},{"test":"Creatinine","result":"3.2","units":"mg/dL","reference":"0.6-1.2","flag":"H"},{"test":"Glucose","result":"128","units":"mg/dL","reference":"70-100","flag":"H"},{"test":"Calcium","result":"8.9","units":"mg/dL","reference":"8.5-10.5","flag":""}],"footnote":"Reference ranges per institutional standards"}}]','[{"toolCallId":"call_-7145216445276746037","toolName":"render_lab_panel","content":"{\\"url\\":\\"/generated/lab-7b247d53-0d76.svg\\",\\"width\\":786,\\"height\\":414,\\"rows\\":8,\\"note\\":\\"Lab panel image saved. Use this exact URL as the question''s imageUrl, and ALSO include the key values as a compact plain-text table in the question text.\\"}","isError":false}]',NULL,'2026-10-21T17:32:43.732Z');
