The questions are now pending review in your question bank. They cover fundamental concepts about skeletal system function and bone structure types.','[{"id":"call_-7145209229731687061","name":"run_question_generation_agent","args":{"topic":"bone anatomy","system":"General","types":["mcq"],"difficulties":["Easy"],"count":2,"focusHint":"simple MCQs about basic bone anatomy","useKnowledgeBase":false}},{"id":"call_-7145166108260035858","name":"task","args":{"description":"Generate exactly 2 easy MCQ questions about basic bone anatomy for a General medical system. The questions should be simple and focus on fundamental bone anatomy concepts. Return the questions as a strict JSON array with complete explanations, citations, and all required fields for the save_question tool.","subagent_type":"question-author"}},{"id":"search_medical_references-1-1792631268195","name":"search_medical_references","args":{"query":"basic bone anatomy structure classification","maxResults":3}},{"id":"call_-7145209126652470227","name":"save_question","args":{"type":"mcq","text":"Which of the following is the primary function of the skeletal system?","options":["Production of red blood cells","Storage of calcium and phosphorus","Protection of internal organs","All of the above"],"answer":"All of the above","explanation":"The skeletal system serves multiple functions including protection of internal organs (e.g., skull protects brain, rib cage protects heart and lungs), production of red blood cells in the bone marrow (hematopoiesis), and storage of calcium and phosphorus as a mineral reservoir. These are all primary functions of the skeletal system.","mnemonic":"POEM - Protection, Organ support, Endocrine functions, Mineral storage","clinicalPearl":"Bone marrow produces approximately 2-3 million red blood cells per second in healthy adults.","distractorAnalysis":"Options A, B, and C each represent individual functions of the skeletal system, but the question asks for the primary function, which encompasses all these roles.","difficulty":"Easy","system":"General","topic":"Bone Anatomy","tags":["skeletal system","bone functions","basic anatomy"],"imageUrl":"","audioUrl":"","illustrationDescription":"","attachSourceMediaId":"","citations":[]}},{"id":"call_-7145180058313813741","name":"save_question","args":{"type":"mcq","text":"Which type of bone is characterized by having a shaft and two expanded ends?","options":["Flat bones","Irregular bones","Long bones","Short bones"],"answer":"Long bones","explanation":"Long bones are characterized by having a cylindrical shaft (diaphysis) and two expanded ends (epiphyses). Examples include the femur, humerus, and tibia. The shaft provides leverage for movement, while the ends contain joints and articular cartilage.","mnemonic":"LEGS - Long bones Extend for Greater movement","clinicalPearl":"Long bones are the most common type of bone in the body and are primarily responsible for weight-bearing and movement.","distractorAnalysis":"Flat bones (like skull bones) provide protection, irregular bones (like vertebrae) have complex shapes, and short bones (like carpals) are cube-shaped - none have the characteristic shaft and expanded ends structure.","difficulty":"Easy","system":"General","topic":"Bone Anatomy","tags":["bone classification","long bones","bone structure"],"imageUrl":"","audioUrl":"","illustrationDescription":"","attachSourceMediaId":"","citations":[]}}]','[{"toolCallId":"search_medical_references-1-1792631268195","toolName":"search_medical_references","content":"{\\"results\\":[],\\"note\\":\\"Web search is temporarily unavailable (no search provider reachable). Answer from your own knowledge, state that live references could not be retrieved, and suggest the user verify current guidance.\\"}","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7145166108260035858","toolName":"task","content":"```json\\n[\\n  {\\n    \\"type\\": \\"mcq\\",\\n    \\"text\\": \\"Which of the following is the primary function of the skeletal system?\\",\\n    \\"options\\": [\\n      \\"Production of red blood cells\\",\\n      \\"Storage of calcium and phosphorus\\",\\n      \\"Protection of internal organs\\",\\n      \\"All of the above\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\"answer\\": \\"D\\",\\n    \\"explanation\\": \\"The skeletal system serves multiple functions including protection of internal organs (e.g., skull protects brain, rib cage protects heart and lungs), production of red blood cells in the bone marrow (hematopoiesis), and storage of calcium and phosphorus as a mineral rese","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7145209126652470227","toolName":"save_question","content":"{\\"saved\\":true,\\"id\\":\\"cmviudov2000nrsu8ib6s5zm3\\",\\"index\\":1,\\"message\\":\\"Question 1 saved (id cmviudov2000nrsu8ib6s5zm3). Continue with the next question or summarize when done.\\"}","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7145180058313813741","toolName":"save_question","content":"{\\"saved\\":true,\\"id\\":\\"cmviuds5l000orsu8ngzah9o5\\",\\"index\\":2,\\"message\\":\\"Question 2 saved (id cmviuds5l000orsu8ngzah9o5). Continue with the next question or summarize when done.\\"}","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7145209229731687061","toolName":"run_question_generation_agent","content":"{\\"ok\\":true,\\"savedCount\\":2,\\"requestedCount\\":2,\\"questions\\":[{\\"index\\":1,\\"id\\":\\"cmviudov2000nrsu8ib6s5zm3\\",\\"type\\":\\"mcq\\",\\"system\\":\\"General\\",\\"topic\\":\\"Bone Anatomy\\",\\"difficulty\\":\\"Easy\\",\\"preview\\":\\"Which of the following is the primary function of the skeletal system?\\"},{\\"index\\":2,\\"id\\":\\"cmviuds5l000orsu8ngzah9o5\\",\\"type\\":\\"mcq\\",\\"system\\":\\"General\\",\\"topic\\":\\"Bone Anatomy\\",\\"difficulty\\":\\"Easy\\",\\"preview\\":\\"Which type of bone is characterized by having a shaft and two expanded ends?\\"}],\\"note\\":\\"Summarize what was saved (count + topics + difficulty) and remind the user the new questions are pending review in the question bank.\\"}","isError":false}]',NULL,'2026-10-22T01:08:07.280Z');
