These cards are now due for immediate review and will resurface at expanding intervals as you rate your recall using the spaced repetition system. You can find them in your Flashcards page where you''ll see a total of 4 cards due now (including the previous metformin contraindication card).','[{"id":"call_-7142205089086697917","name":"create_flashcards","args":{"cards":[{"front":"Metformin''s primary mechanism of action","back":"Activates AMP-activated protein kinase (AMPK), leading to decreased hepatic glucose production and increased insulin sensitivity","system":"Endocrine","topic":"Metformin mechanism of action"},{"front":"How does metformin affect glucose uptake in peripheral tissues?","back":"Increases glucose uptake in skeletal muscle and adipose tissue by enhancing insulin sensitivity and translocation of GLUT4 transporters to the cell membrane","system":"Endocrine","topic":"Metformin mechanism of action"},{"front":"What is metformin''s effect on intestinal glucose absorption?","back":"Decreases intestinal glucose absorption by inhibiting glucose transporters (SGLT1) in the intestinal mucosa","system":"Endocrine","topic":"Metformin mechanism of action"}],"deckLabel":"Metformin mechanism of action"}}]','[{"toolCallId":"call_-7142205089086697917","toolName":"create_flashcards","content":"{\\"created\\":true,\\"count\\":3,\\"cards\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"cmvlxufdx000sbbrdm5grzusg\\",\\"front\\":\\"Metformin''s primary mechanism of action\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"cmvlxufe9000vbbrd61g7hz7c\\",\\"front\\":\\"How does metformin affect glucose uptake in peripheral tissues?\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"cmvlxufec000xbbrdd7d23s6g\\",\\"front\\":\\"What is metformin''s effect on intestinal glucose absorption?\\"}],\\"totalDueNow\\":4,\\"note\\":\\"Saved 3 flashcards to the learner''s review queue. Tell them the cards are due NOW (4 total due) on the Flashcards page, and SM-2 will resurface each card at expanding intervals as they rate their recall.\\"}","isError":false}]',NULL,'2026-10-24T05:08:21.420Z');
