','[{"id":"call_-7142200106924638115","name":"search_medical_references","args":{"query":"sepsis pathophysiology cytokine cascade organ dysfunction mechanisms management guidelines","maxResults":5}},{"id":"call_-7142205020367222725","name":"search_medical_references","args":{"query":"sepsis management guidelines Sepsis-3 bundle fluid resuscitation antibiotics","maxResults":4}}]','[{"toolCallId":"call_-7142200106924638115","toolName":"search_medical_references","content":"{\\"results\\":[{\\"title\\":\\"Septic Shock: Background, Definitions of Key Terms,\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/168402-overview\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Sepsis is defined as life-threatening organ dysfunction due to dysregulated host response to infection. Organ dysfunction Sepsis is described ...\\",\\"host\\":\\"emedicine.medscape.com\\",\\"date\\":\\"Aug 19, 2026\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Sepsis—Pathophysiology and Therapeutic Concepts - PMC\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8160230\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"by D Jarczak · 2021 · Cited by 692 — Sepsis is a life-threatening condition and a global disease burden. is defined as severe organ dysfunction caused by a dysregulated host response to infection, ...\\",\\"host\\":\\"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Cytokines in sepsis: a critical review of the literature on\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/immunology/articles/10.3389/fimmu.2025.1682306/full\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"by R Vella · 2025 · Cited by 59 — Sepsis arises from a dysregulated immune response, characterized by an initial hyperinflammatory phase followed by a state of immunosuppression, both of which ...\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.frontiersin.org\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Sepsis and Septic Shock - Critical Care Medicine\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/critical-care-medicine/sepsis-and-septic-shock/sepsis-and-septic-shock\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Sepsis is a clinical syndrome of life-threatening organ dysfunction caused by a dysregulated host response to infection. These cytokines cause neutrophil– ...\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.merckmanuals.com\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Understanding Sepsis-Induced Multiple Organ Dysfunction\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.mdpi.com/1422-0067/25/14/7770\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"by T Srdić · 2024 · Cited by 201 — Sepsis-induced multiple organ dysfunction arises from the highly complex pathophysiology encompassing the interplay of inflammation, oxidative ...\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.mdpi.com\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"}],\\"formatted\\":\\"[S1] Septic Shock: Background, Definitions of Key Terms, (Aug 19, 2026)\\\\n    https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/168402-overview (emedicine.medscape.com)\\\\n    Sepsis is defined as life-threatening organ dysfunction due to dysregulated host response to infection. Organ dysfunction Sepsis is described ...\\\\n[S2] Sepsis—Pathophysiology and Therapeutic Concepts - PMC\\\\n    https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8160230 (pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov)\\\\n    by D Jarczak · 2021 · Cited by 692 — Sepsis is a life-threatening condition and a global disease burden. is defined as severe organ dysfunction caused by a dysregulated host response to infection, ...\\\\n[S3] Cytokines in sepsis: a critical review of the literature on\\\\n    https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/immunology/articles/10.3389/fimmu.2025.1682306/full (www.frontiersin.org)\\\\n    by R Vella · 2025 · Cited by 59 — Sepsis arises from a dysregulated immune response, characterized by an initial hyperinflammatory phase followed by a state of immunosuppression, both of which ...\\\\n[S4] Sepsis and Septic Shock - Critical Care Medicine\\\\n    https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/critical-care-medicine/sepsis-and-septic-shock/sepsis-and-septic-shock (www.merckmanuals.com)\\\\n    Sepsis is a clinical syndrome of life-threatening organ dysfunction caused by a dysregulated host response to infection. These cytokines cause neutrophil– ...\\\\n[S5] Understanding Sepsis-Induced Multiple Organ Dysfunction\\\\n    https://www.mdpi.com/1422-0067/25/14/7770 (www.mdpi.com)\\\\n    by T Srdić · 2024 · Cited by 201 — Sepsis-induced multiple organ dysfunction arises from the highly complex pathophysiology encompassing the interplay of inflammation, oxidative ...\\",\\"note\\":\\"Cite these inline as [S1], [S2]… markers placed right after the claim each source supports. NEVER paste raw URLs into the answer text — the interface renders [S#] markers as clickable source cards and lists every URL in a Web sources panel automatically. Results are re-ranked for recency (freshest first): when a source carries a date, mention the year the moment you cite it (e.g. \\\\\\"per t","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142205020367222725","toolName":"search_medical_references","content":"{\\"results\\":[{\\"title\\":\\"Evaluation and management of suspected sepsis and\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.uptodate.com/contents/evaluation-and-management-of-suspected-sepsis-and-septic-shock-in-adults\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"May 7, 2026 — Empiric antibiotic therapy is targeted at the suspected organism(s ) and site(s) of infection and preferably administered within the first hour. Read more\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.uptodate.com\\",\\"date\\":\\"May 7, 2026\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Hospital Sepsis Program Core Elements\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.cdc.gov/sepsis/hcp/core-elements/index.html\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Sep 21, 2026 — This document summarizes Core Elements of hospital sepsis programs, which are intended to monitor and optimize hospital management and outcomes ... Read more\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.cdc.gov\\",\\"date\\":\\"Sep 21, 2026\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Surviving Sepsis Campaign Adult Guidelines\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://sccm.org/survivingsepsiscampaign/guidelines-and-resources/surviving-sepsis-campaign-adult-guidelines\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"For adults with probable or definite sepsis without shock, we “recommend” administering antimicrobial therapy immediately, ideally within 1 hr of recognition. Read more\\",\\"host\\":\\"sccm.org\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Surviving sepsis campaign: international guidelines for  - PMC\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8486643\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"by L Evans · 2021 · Cited by 10843 — The 2016 SSC guideline issued a recommendation for using a minimum of 30 ml/kg (ideal body weight) of IV crystalloids in initial fluid resuscitation . This fixed ... Read more\\",\\"host\\":\\"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"}],\\"formatted\\":\\"[S1] Evaluation and management of suspected sepsis and (May 7, 2026)\\\\n    https://www.uptodate.com/contents/evaluation-and-management-of-suspected-sepsis-and-septic-shock-in-adults (www.uptodate.com)\\\\n    May 7, 2026 — Empiric antibiotic therapy is targeted at the suspected organism(s ) and site(s) of infection and preferably administered within the first hour. Read more\\\\n[S2] Hospital Sepsis Program Core Elements (Sep 21, 2026)\\\\n    https://www.cdc.gov/sepsis/hcp/core-elements/index.html (www.cdc.gov)\\\\n    Sep 21, 2026 — This document summarizes Core Elements of hospital sepsis programs, which are intended to monitor and optimize hospital management and outcomes ... Read more\\\\n[S3] Surviving Sepsis Campaign Adult Guidelines\\\\n    https://sccm.org/survivingsepsiscampaign/guidelines-and-resources/surviving-sepsis-campaign-adult-guidelines (sccm.org)\\\\n    For adults with probable or definite sepsis without shock, we “recommend” administering antimicrobial therapy immediately, ideally within 1 hr of recognition. Read more\\\\n[S4] Surviving sepsis campaign: international guidelines for  - PMC\\\\n    https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8486643 (pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov)\\\\n    by L Evans · 2021 · Cited by 10843 — The 2016 SSC guideline issued a recommendation for using a minimum of 30 ml/kg (ideal body weight) of IV crystalloids in initial fluid resuscitation . This fixed ... Read more\\",\\"note\\":\\"Cite these inline as [S1], [S2]… markers placed right after the claim each source supports. NEVER paste raw URLs into the answer text — the interface renders [S#] markers as clickable source cards and lists every URL in a Web sources panel automatically. Results are re-ranked for recency (freshest first): when a source carries a date, mention the year the moment you cite it (e.g. \\\\\\"per the 2024 ESC guideline [S1]\\\\\\"), and prefer the most recent guidance when sources conflict — flag older sources as superseded where relevant.\\"}","isError":false}]','{"interrupted":true}','2026-10-24T05:40:33.425Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvlz0bgj000kv6rd75mf92qy','228c86f9-7798-44b5-b9cf-a72f67403045','user','What is the first-line treatment for anaphylaxis?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-24T05:40:53.635Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvlz0ks5000nv6rdccmeidzw','228c86f9-7798-44b5-b9cf-a72f67403045','assistant','I''ll search for current medical guidelines on the first-line treatment for anaphylaxis.

The first-line treatment for anaphylaxis is **intramuscular epinephrine (adrenaline)**.

According to current guidelines from 2022-2024 [S1][S3][S5], epinephrine is universally recognized as the first-line treatment for anaphylaxis. Key points include:

**Administration Details:**
- **Route**: Intramuscular (IM) injection
- **Location**: Anterolateral thigh (preferred site)
- **Dosing**: 0.3-0.5 mg for adults (1:1000 concentration), repeated every 5-15 minutes as needed
- **Timing**: Should be administered immediately when anaphylaxis is suspected

**Important Considerations:**
- IM epinephrine is first-line even if IV access is available [S2]
- A single dose of IM epinephrine is well-tolerated and effective [S2]
- Epinephrine works through both alpha and beta adrenergic receptors to counteract the pathophysiological effects of anaphylaxis [S4]

**Why Epinephrine is First-Line:**
Epinephrine is the only medication that can rapidly reverse the life-threatening aspects of anaphylaxis by:
- Causing vasoconstriction (counteracting vasodilation and hypotension)
- Bronchodilation (relieving bronchospasm)
- Increasing cardiac contractility and heart rate
- Inhibiting further mast cell degranulation
- Reducing vascular permeability

**Additional Treatments:**
While epinephrine is first-line, additional treatments may be needed depending on severity and response:
- Oxygen supplementation
- IV fluids for hypotension
- H1 and H2 antihistamines
- Corticosteroids
- Beta-2 agonists for bronchospasm

The 2023 practice parameter update from the American Academy of Allergy, Asthma & Immunology emphasizes that epinephrine remains the cornerstone of anaphylaxis management [S3][S5].','[{"id":"call_-7142205054726958133","name":"search_medical_references","args":{"query":"first-line treatment anaphylaxis guidelines epinephrine","maxResults":5}}]','[{"toolCallId":"call_-7142205054726958133","toolName":"search_medical_references","content":"{\\"results\\":[{\\"title\\":\\"Emergency treatment of anaphylaxis: concise clinical guidance\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9345203\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"by AF Whyte · 2022 · Cited by 87 — IM adrenaline is the first-line treatment for anaphylaxis (Fig 2). There are no randomised trials evaluating adrenaline to treat anaphylaxis, however, extensive ... Read more\\",\\"host\\":\\"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Emergency treatment of anaphylaxis Guidelines for\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.resus.org.uk/sites/default/files/2021-05/Emergency%20Treatment%20of%20Anaphylaxis%20May%202021_0.pdf\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Intramuscular adrenaline is the first-line treatment for anaphylaxis (even if intravenous access is available). • A single dose of IM adrenaline is well- ... Read more\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.resus.org.uk\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Anaphylaxis: A 2023 practice parameter update\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.aaaai.org/Aaaai/media/Media-Library-PDFs/Allergist%20Resources/Statements%20and%20Practice%20Parameters/Anaphylaxis-Practice-Paramaters-2023.pdf\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"by DBK Golden · 2023 · Cited by 468 — Epinephrine is the first-line treatment for anaphylaxis , and EAIs allow patients to have this emergency medication available outside the medical setting.\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.aaaai.org\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Anaphylaxis Clinical Pathway\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.hopkinsmedicine.org/-/media/files/allchildrens/clinical-pathways/anaphylaxis-pathway-7_2023.pdf\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Intramuscular EPINEPHrine is the first line treatment for anaphylaxis (Class I, Level of Evidence A). EPINEPHrine has both alpha sympathomimetic and beta. ...\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.hopkinsmedicine.org\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Anaphylaxis: A 2023 practice parameter update\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.annallergy.org/article/S1081-1206(23)01304-2/fulltext\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"by DBK Golden · 2024 · Cited by 468 — Epinephrine is the first-line treatment for anaphylaxis , and EAIs allow patients to have this emergency medication available outside the ...\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.annallergy.org\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"}],\\"formatted\\":\\"[S1] Emergency treatment of anaphylaxis: concise clinical guidance\\\\n    https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9345203 (pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov)\\\\n    by AF Whyte · 2022 · Cited by 87 — IM adrenaline is the first-line treatment for anaphylaxis (Fig 2). There are no randomised trials evaluating adrenaline to treat anaphylaxis, however, extensive ... Read more\\\\n[S2] Emergency treatment of anaphylaxis Guidelines for\\\\n    https://www.resus.org.uk/sites/default/files/2021-05/Emergency%20Treatment%20of%20Anaphylaxis%20May%202021_0.pdf (www.resus.org.uk)\\\\n    Intramuscular adrenaline is the first-line treatment for anaphylaxis (even if intravenous access is available). • A single dose of IM adrenaline is well- ... Read more\\\\n[S3] Anaphylaxis: A 2023 practice parameter update\\\\n    https://www.aaaai.org/Aaaai/media/Media-Library-PDFs/Allergist%20Resources/Statements%20and%20Practice%20Parameters/Anaphylaxis-Practice-Paramaters-2023.pdf (www.aaaai.org)\\\\n    by DBK Golden · 2023 · Cited by 468 — Epinephrine is the first-line treatment for anaphylaxis , and EAIs allow patients to have this emergency medication available outside the medical setting.\\\\n[S4] Anaphylaxis Clinical Pathway\\\\n    https://www.hopkinsmedicine.org/-/media/files/allchildrens/clinical-pathways/anaphylaxis-pathway-7_2023.pdf (www.hopkinsmedicine.org)\\\\n    Intramuscular EPINEPHrine is the first line treatment for anaphylaxis (Class I, Level of Evidence A). EPINEPHrine has both alpha sympathomimetic and beta. ...\\\\n[S5] Anaphylaxis: A 2023 practice parameter update\\\\n    https://www.annallergy.org/article/S1081-1206(23)01304-2/fulltext (www.annallergy.org)\\\\n    by DBK Golden · 2024 · Cited by 468 — Epinephrine is the first-line treatment for anaphylaxis , and EAIs allow patients to have this emergency medication available outside the ...\\",\\"note\\":\\"Cite these inline as [S1], [S2]… markers placed right after the claim each source supports. NEVER paste raw URLs into the answer text — the interface renders [","isError":false}]',NULL,'2026-10-24T05:41:05.717Z');
