INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvm06e340003wnrd85xlxslf','57919e5f-935e-4374-9fc4-6d2983054c72','user','What is the latest research on CAR-T cell therapy? Please cite sources with links.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-24T06:13:36.430Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvm06trk0007wnrdwhv608k0','57919e5f-935e-4374-9fc4-6d2983054c72','assistant','I''ll search for the latest research on CAR-T cell therapy for you.

Here''s the latest research on CAR-T cell therapy based on current sources:

## Current Clinical Landscape

**Global Clinical Trials Progress**
As of April 2024, there are 1,580 CAR-T clinical trials registered globally [S4]. Recent analysis shows significant expansion into solid tumors, with particular focus on:
- Liver, gallbladder, and pancreas cancers (14.8% of solid tumor trials)
- Esophageal and gastric cancers [S3]

**Recent Clinical Trial Initiatives**
- **Mayo Clinic** (July 2025): Currently conducting 8 active CAR-T clinical trials [S1]
- **KU Cancer Center** (August 2025): Launched a "Triple Threat" CAR-T therapy in a Phase 1 first-in-human clinical trial [S2]

## Major Advances in Solid Tumors

**September 2025 Breakthrough**
Mayo Clinic researchers announced a promising breakthrough in CAR-T therapy for solid tumors, representing a significant advance in this challenging area [S3].

**2025 ASCO Meeting Advances**
Recent phase I clinical trial advances for solid tumors were highlighted at the 2025 ASCO Meeting, showing progress in multi-antigen targeting strategies [S2]. The review examines successful clinical trials in advanced solid tumors and focuses on approaches to enhance CAR efficacy [S1].

## Research Focus Areas

Current research emphasizes:
- **Multi-antigen targeting** to overcome tumor heterogeneity
- **Enhanced CAR design** for better tumor penetration and persistence
- **Overcoming the immunosuppressive tumor microenvironment**

## Market and Development Trends

The CAR-T cell therapy market is experiencing significant growth, with forecasts showing continued expansion through 2025. Several late-stage clinical trials are approaching commercialization, suggesting new therapies may soon become available [S5].

These sources represent the most current research landscape as of mid-2025, with ongoing evolution in both clinical applications and therapeutic approaches.','[{"id":"call_-7142183339372313898","name":"search_medical_references","args":{"query":"CAR-T cell therapy latest research 2024 2025 clinical trials","maxResults":5}},{"id":"call_-7142194712445709373","name":"search_medical_references","args":{"query":"CAR-T cell therapy solid tumors 2025 recent advances","maxResults":3}}]','[{"toolCallId":"call_-7142183339372313898","toolName":"search_medical_references","content":"{\\"results\\":[{\\"title\\":\\"CAR-T Cell Therapy Program - Clinical trials\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.mayoclinic.org/departments-centers/car-t-cell-therapy-program/sections/clinical-trials/rsc-20405550\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Jul 19, 2025 — Below are current clinical trials . 8 studies in CAR-T Cell Therapy Program (open studies only). Filter this list of studies by location, status ...\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.mayoclinic.org\\",\\"date\\":\\"Jul 19, 2025\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Triple Threat CAR T-Cell Therapy Trial\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.kucancercenter.org/news-room/news/2025/08/triple-threat-car-tcell-therapy-clinical-trial-debuts-at-ku-cancer-center\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Aug 5, 2025 — A new type of CAR T-cell therapy dubbed Triple Threat, currently under evaluation via a Phase 1, first-in-human clinical trial initiated by ... Read more\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.kucancercenter.org\\",\\"date\\":\\"Aug 5, 2025\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"CAR-T cell therapy clinical trials: global progress\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/immunology/articles/10.3389/fimmu.2025.1583116/full\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"by LY Cao · 2025 · Cited by 70 — The CAR - T trials in solid tumors mainly focus on the liver, gallbladder, and pancreas (14.8%); esophagus, stomach solid tumors field, with MESO ...\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.frontiersin.org\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"CAR-T cell therapy clinical trials: global progress,