ayo Clinic have made a promising breakthrough in the development of a novel therapy for solid tumor treatment.\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.mayoclinic.org\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"}],\\"formatted\\":\\"[S1] CAR-T cells in solid tumors: Challenges and breakthroughs\\\\n    https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2666379125004264 (www.sciencedirect.com)\\\\n    We examine recent successful clinical trials in advanced solid tumors and highlight strategies to enable multi-antigen targeting and enhance CAR ...\\\\n[S2] Emerging advances in CAR-T therapy for solid tumors - PMC\\\\n    https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12628604 (pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov)\\\\n    In this review, we highlight the main phase I clinical trial advances in CAR-T therapy for solid tumors presented at the 2025 ASCO Meeting.\\\\n[S3] Major advance in use of CAR-T cell therapy to treat solid tumors\\\\n    https://www.mayoclinic.org/medical-professionals/cancer/news/major-advance-in-use-of-car-t-cell-therapy-to-treat-solid-tumors/mac-20588405 (www.mayoclinic.org)\\\\n    Sept. 03, 2025 Researchers at Mayo Clinic have made a promising breakthrough in the development of a novel therapy for solid tumor treatment.\\",\\"note\\":\\"Cite these inline as [S1], [S2]… markers placed right after the claim each source supports. NEVER paste raw URLs into the answer text — the interface renders [S#] markers as clickable source cards and lists every URL in a Web sources panel automatically. Results are re-ranked for recency (freshest first): when a source carries a date, mention the year the moment you cite it (e.g. \\\\\\"per the 2024 ESC guideline [S1]\\\\\\"), and prefer the most recent guidance when sources conflict — flag older sources as superseded where relevant.\\"}","isError":false}]',NULL,'2026-10-24T06:13:56.912Z');
