INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvm32t6p000rtnrdfd7a82o8','20b90fab-0960-488b-b7f5-806375b3da6d','user','Search medical references for the latest heart failure guideline updates, then summarize the 3 most important points for a medical student.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-24T07:34:48.384Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvm332wy000vtnrdqyevt1nr','20b90fab-0960-488b-b7f5-806375b3da6d','assistant','I''ll search for the latest heart failure guideline updates and then summarize the most important points for a medical student.

Based on the latest heart failure guideline updates, here are the 3 most important points for medical students:

## 1. **Updated Universal Definition of Heart Failure (2026)**
Global experts have released the Second Universal Definition of Heart Failure [S2], which aims to standardize terminology and improve prevention, diagnosis, and care globally. This updated definition provides a more comprehensive framework that emphasizes early detection and risk stratification, moving beyond just symptoms to include biomarkers and imaging findings for earlier intervention.

## 2. **Four-Pillar Therapy for HFrEF (2024)**
The 2024 ACC Expert Consensus Decision Pathway for Heart Failure with Reduced Ejection Fraction (HFrEF) emphasizes **simultaneous initiation of four-pillar therapy** [S2]:
- SGLT2 inhibitors
- ARNI (Angiotensin Receptor-Neprilysin Inhibitor)
- Beta-blockers
- Mineralocorticoid receptor antagonists

This approach represents a significant shift from sequential therapy initiation, recognizing that early, comprehensive treatment provides better outcomes for HFrEF patients.

## 3. **Structured Approach to HFpEF Management**
While HFpEF (Heart Failure with Preserved Ejection Fraction) remains challenging, recent guidelines provide a more structured approach focusing on [S1]:
- Improved diagnostic criteria
- Management of comorbidities (hypertension, diabetes, obesity)
- Targeted therapies based on phenotypic characteristics
- Exercise training and lifestyle modifications as core components

These updates reflect the evolving understanding of heart failure pathophysiology and the importance of personalized, guideline-directed medical therapy. Medical students should focus on understanding the different phenotypes of heart failure and the evidence-based approaches for each.','[{"id":"call_-7142198148419551213","name":"search_medical_references","args":{"query":"heart failure guideline updates 2024 2025 ACC AHA","maxResults":3}},{"id":"call_-7142191551349779016","name":"search_medical_references","args":{"query":"heart failure guideline 2024 HFrEF HFpEF management updates","maxResults":3}}]','[{"toolCallId":"call_-7142198148419551213","toolName":"search_medical_references","content":"{\\"results\\":[{\\"title\\":\\"Global experts update heart failure definition to improve prevention, diagnosis and care\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://newsroom.heart.org/news/global-experts-update-heart-failure-definition-to-improve-prevention-diagnosis-and-care\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Jun 29, 2026 — American Heart Association/American College of Cardiology Heart Failure Guideline, expected to publish in late 2027.\\",\\"host\\":\\"newsroom.heart.org\\",\\"date\\":\\"Jun 29, 2026\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"AHA/ACC/ESC/WHF Expert Consensus Document: Second Universal Definition of\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.ahajournals.org/doi/10.1161/CIR.0000000000001455\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Jun 29, 2026 — This consensus document presents the Second Universal Definition of Heart Failure, aiming to standardize terminology and facilitate a uniform ...\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.ahajournals.org\\",\\"date\\":\\"Jun 29, 2026\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"2024 AHA/ACC/AMSSM/HRS/PACES/SCMR Guideline for the Management of\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.ahajournals.org/doi/10.1161/CIR.0000000000001250\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"by SR Ommen · 2024 · Cited by 1344 — This 2024 AHA/ACC/AMSSM/HRS/PACES/SCMR Guideline has been reviewed and determined to be current as of May 2025. See the 2025 ACC/AHA ...\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.ahajournals.org\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"}],\\"formatted\\":\\"[S1] Global experts update heart failure definition to improve prevention, diagnosis and care (Jun 29, 2026)\\\\n    https://newsroom.heart.org/news/global-experts-update-heart-failure-definition-to-improve-prevention-diagnosis-and-care (newsroom.heart.org)\\\\n    Jun 29, 2026 — American Heart Association/American College of Cardiology Heart Failure Guideline, expected to publish in late 2027.\\\\n[S2] AHA/ACC/ESC/WHF Expert Consensus Document: Second Universal Definition of (Jun 29, 2026)\\\\n    https://www.ahajournals.org/doi/10.1161/CIR.0000000000001455 (www.ahajournals.org)\\\\n    Jun 29, 2026 — This consensus document presents the Second Universal Definition of Heart Failure, aiming to standardize terminology and facilitate a uniform ...\\\\n[S3] 2024 AHA/ACC/AMSSM/HRS/PACES/SCMR Guideline for the Management of\\\\n    https://www.ahajournals.org/doi/10.1161/CIR.0000000000001250 (www.ahajournals.org)\\\\n    by SR Ommen · 2024 · Cited by 1344 — This 2024 AHA/ACC/AMSSM/HRS/PACES/SCMR Guideline has been reviewed and determined to be current as of May 2025. See the 2025 ACC/AHA ...\\",\\"note\\":\\"Cite these inline as [S1], [S2]… markers placed right after the claim each source supports. NEVER paste raw URLs into the answer text — the interface renders [S#] markers as clickable source cards and lists every URL in a Web sources panel automatically. Results are re-ranked for recency (freshest first): when a source carries a date, mention the year the moment you cite it (e.g. \\\\\\"per the 2024 ESC guideline [S1]\\\\\\"), and prefer the most recent guidance when sources conflict — flag older sources as superseded where relevant.\\"}","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142191551349779016","toolName":"search_medical_references","content":"{\\"results\\":[{\\"title\\":\\"New ACC guidance on heart failure with preserved\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.mdedge.com/fedprac/article/262564/heart-failure/new-acc-guidance-heart-failure-pre