54364-overview\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Oct 17, 2025 — Adults/older adults: 3.5-5.0 mEq/L or 3.5-5.0 mmol/L (SI units) Children: 3.4-4.7 mEq/L Infants: 4.1-5.3 mEq/L Newborns: 3.9-5.9 mEq/L\\",\\"host\\":\\"emedicine.medscape.com\\",\\"date\\":\\"Oct 17, 2025\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Potassium Blood Test\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/potassium-blood-test\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Nov 12, 2024 — Learn more about laboratory tests, reference ranges , and understanding results. Is there anything else I need to know about a potassium blood ... Read more\\",\\"host\\":\\"medlineplus.gov\\",\\"date\\":\\"Nov 12, 2024\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Serum Potassium - Clinical Methods - NCBI Bookshelf - NIH\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK307\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"by A Rastegar · 1990 · Cited by 99 — Normal serum potassium is 3.5 to 5.5 mEq/L ; however, plasma potassium is 0.5 mEq/L lower. While total body potassium is lower in females and in older patients, ... Read more\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"}],\\"formatted\\":\\"[S1] Potassium: Reference Range, Interpretation, Collection (Oct 17, 2025)\\\\n    https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/2054364-overview (emedicine.medscape.com)\\\\n    Oct 17, 2025 — Adults/older adults: 3.5-5.0 mEq/L or 3.5-5.0 mmol/L (SI units) Children: 3.4-4.7 mEq/L Infants: 4.1-5.3 mEq/L Newborns: 3.9-5.9 mEq/L\\\\n[S2] Potassium Blood Test (Nov 12, 2024)\\\\n    https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/potassium-blood-test (medlineplus.gov)\\\\n    Nov 12, 2024 — Learn more about laboratory tests, reference ranges , and understanding results. Is there anything else I need to know about a potassium blood ... Read more\\\\n[S3] Serum Potassium - Clinical Methods - NCBI Bookshelf - NIH\\\\n    https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK307 (www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov)\\\\n    by A Rastegar · 1990 · Cited by 99 — Normal serum potassium is 3.5 to 5.5 mEq/L ; however, plasma potassium is 0.5 mEq/L lower. While total body potassium is lower in females and in older patients, ... Read more\\",\\"note\\":\\"Cite these inline as [S1], [S2]… markers placed right after the claim each source supports. NEVER paste raw URLs into the answer text — the interface renders [S#] markers as clickable source cards and lists every URL in a Web sources panel automatically. Results are re-ranked for recency (freshest first): when a source carries a date, mention the year the moment you cite it (e.g. \\\\\\"per the 2024 ESC guideline [S1]\\\\\\"), and prefer the most recent guidance when sources conflict — flag older sources as superseded where relevant.\\"}","isError":false}]',NULL,'2026-10-24T08:41:18.431Z');
