You can access your anion gap study note anytime by reading the file at `/anion-gap-notes.md`.','[{"id":"call_d723ed5c680349d1956987cc","name":"write_file","args":{"content":"# Anion Gap Study Notes\\n\\n## Normal Range\\n- **Current standard**: 3-11 mEq/L\\n- **Historical range**: 8-12 mEq/L\\n\\n## Definition\\nThe anion gap represents the difference between measured cations and anions in the blood:\\n- **Formula**: Anion Gap = Na⁺ - (Cl⁻ + HCO₃⁻)\\n- **Alternative formula** (includes K⁺): Anion Gap = (Na⁺ + K⁺) - (Cl⁻ + HCO₃⁻)\\n\\n## Clinical Significance\\n- **Elevated anion gap**: Indicates metabolic acidosis with unmeasured anions\\n- **Normal anion gap**: Suggests non-gap metabolic acidosis or other electrolyte imbalances\\n\\n## Mnemonic for Elevated Anion Gap (MUDPILES)\\n- **M**ethanol\\n- **U**remia\\n- **D**iabetic ketoacidosis\\n- **P**araldehyde\\n- **I**soniazid\\n- **L**actic acidosis\\n- **E**thylene glycol\\n- **S**alicylates\\n\\n## Important Notes\\n- Always verify with your specific laboratory''s reference range\\n- Modern techniques have lowered the normal range from older references\\n- Clinical interpretation should consider the patient''s overall clinical picture","file_path":"/anion-gap-notes.md"}},{"id":"call_0508b8678eaa4d86b69afd29","name":"write_file","args":{"content":"# Test Skill\\n\\n## Description\\nThis is a test skill file to verify the skills directory functionality.\\n\\n## When to Use\\nUse this skill for testing purposes only.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n1. This is a test skill\\n2. It contains basic markdown content\\n3. It demonstrates the skills directory structure\\n\\n## Output Format\\nPlain text output with skill information.\\n\\n## Notes\\nThis is a test file created for verification purposes.","file_path":"/skills/test-skill/SKILL.md"}}]','[{"toolCallId":"call_d723ed5c680349d1956987cc","toolName":"write_file","content":"Successfully wrote to ''/anion-gap-notes.md''","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_0508b8678eaa4d86b69af