INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvmdg02t0016e3rdy750o73a','7b60b22c-efc1-4cf3-8dc1-35772dcf44b1','user','Quick question, no tools needed: according to my AGENTS.md, which units should you use and how should you explain answers? Answer in one sentence.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-24T12:25:00.005Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvmf3ves000byjrdwsr1uy3a','7e053ffc-11d9-4ffe-ac42-f8e97cb7fd5d','assistant','I''ll create a personalized 4-week USMLE Step 1 study plan based on your real quiz performance. Let me first analyze your weaknesses and get the exam blueprint to create an effective plan.

Based on your real quiz performance and the USMLE Step 1 exam blueprint, here''s your personalized 4-week study plan:

## Your Performance Analysis
**Overall Accuracy:** 0% (40 attempts)
**Weakest Topics (0% accuracy):**
- ACE inhibitors (4 attempts)
- Constipation (2 attempts) 
- Hirschsprung Disease (2 attempts)
- Platelet Disorders (2 attempts)
- Rickets (2 attempts)
- Tracheo-esophageal Fistula (2 attempts)

**Weakest Systems (0% accuracy):**
- General (4 attempts)
- Gastroenterology/Gastrointestinal (2 attempts each)
- Endocrinology/Endocrine (2 attempts each)

## 4-Week USMLE Step 1 Study Plan

### Week 1: Foundation & High-Yield Systems (28% weight)
**Focus Areas:** General Principles (14%) + Behavioral Health/Nervous System (13%)

**Daily Structure:**
- **Morning (3 hours):** General Principles review
  - Biochemistry pathways
  - Cell biology fundamentals  
  - Genetics basics
  - Immunology foundations

- **Afternoon (3 hours):** Behavioral Health & Nervous System
  - Neuroanatomy & physiology
  - Psychopharmacology
  - Behavioral science concepts

- **Evening (2 hours):** Targeted weak topics practice
  - ACE inhibitors mechanisms & side effects
  - Platelet disorders pathophysiology

### Week 2: Musculoskeletal & Respiratory/Renal (28% weight)
**Focus Areas:** Musculoskeletal/Skin (11%) + Respiratory/Renal (17%)

**Daily Structure:**
- **Morning (3 hours):** Musculoskeletal & Skin
  - Bone physiology & pathology
  - Connective tissue disorders
  - Dermatology conditions

- **Afternoon (3 hours):** Respiratory & Renal/Urinary
  - Pulmonary physiology & diseases
  - Renal physiology & pathologies
  - Acid-base balance

- **Evening (2 hours):** Targeted weak topics practice
  - Rickets (vitamin D metabolism & bone disorders)
  - Constipation pathophysiology & management

### Week 3: Cardiovascular & Gastrointestinal (19% weight)
**Focus Areas:** Cardiovascular (10%) + Gastrointestinal (9%)

**Daily Structure:**
- **Morning (3 hours):** Cardiovascular System
  - Cardiac physiology & pharmacology
  - Hypertension & arrhythmias
  - Coronary artery disease

- **Afternoon (3 hours):** Gastrointestinal System
  - GI physiology & motility
  - Liver & pancreatic diseases
  - GI infections & inflammation

- **Evening (2 hours):** Targeted weak topics practice
  - Hirschsprung Disease (congenital GI disorders)
  - Tracheo-esophageal Fistula (congenital anomalies)

### Week 4: Endocrine & Multisystem + Comprehensive Review (16% weight)
**Focus Areas:** Endocrine (8%) + Multisystem (8%) + Final Review

**Daily Structure:**
- **Morning (2 hours):** Endocrine System
  - Hormone mechanisms & receptors
  - Diabetes & endocrine disorders
  - Thyroid & adrenal diseases

- **Afternoon (2 hours):** Multisystem Processes
  - Sepsis & systemic inflammatory responses
  - Metabolic disorders
  - Toxicology

- **Evening (3 hours):** Comprehensive weak topics review
  - All previously identified weak areas
  - Practice questions & case studies
  - High-yield mnemonics & clinical correlations

## Special Focus on Your Weakest Areas

**Targeted Practice Sessions:**
- **ACE inhibitors:** Daily 30-minute deep dive (mechanisms, side effects, clinical applications)
- **Constipation:** Pathophysiology review + treatment algorithms
- **Hirschsprung Disease:** Embryology, clinical presentation, diagnosis, management
- **Platelet Disorders:** Coagulation cascade, bleeding disorders, thrombocytopenia
- **Rickets:** Vitamin D metabolism, bone development, prevention/treatment
- **Tracheo-esophageal Fistula:** Embryology, diagnosis, surgical management

## Recommended Study Strategies

1. **Active Recall:** Use flashcards for key concepts
2. **Spaced Repetition:** Review material at expanding intervals
3. **Practice Questions:** 50-100 questions daily focusing on weak areas
4. **Clinical Correlations:** Connect basic science to clinical presentations
5. **Teach-Back:** Explain concepts aloud to reinforce understanding

Would you like me to create flashcards for any of your weakest topics, set up a recurring weekly practice schedule, or generate targeted practice questions for specific areas?','[{"id":"call_-7142176123827255624","name":"analyze_my_weaknesses","args":{"limit":8}},{"id":"call_-7142156470056908183","name":"get_exam_blueprint","args":{"exam":"usmle-step1","weeksAvailable":4}},{"id":"call_-7142175711510395705","name":"write_todos","args":{"todos":[{"content":"Create 4-week USMLE Step 1 study plan based on exam blueprint and weak areas","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Week 1: Focus on General Principles (14%) and Behavioral Health/Nervous System (13%) with emphasis on weak topics","status":"pending"},{"content":"Week 2: Focus on Musculoskeletal/Skin (11%) and Respiratory/Renal (17%) with emphasis on weak topics","status":"pending"},{"content":"Week 3: Focus on Cardiovascular (10%) and GI (9%) with emphasis on weak topics","status":"pending"},{"content":"Week 4: Focus on Endocrine (8%) and Multisystem (8%) with emphasis on weak topics","status":"pending"},{"content":"Add targeted practice sessions for weakest topics: ACE inhibitors, Constipation, Hirschsprung Disease, Platelet Disorders, Rickets, Tracheo-esophageal Fistula","status":"pending"}]}},{"id":"call_-7142175264833791253","name":"write_todos","args":{"todos":[{"content":"Create 4-week USMLE Step 1 study plan based on exam blueprint and weak areas","status":"completed"},{"content":"Week 1: Focus on General Principles (14%) and Behavioral Health/Nervous System (13%) with emphasis on weak topics","status":"completed"},{"content":"Week 2: Focus on Musculoskeletal/Skin (11%) and Respiratory/Renal (17%) with emphasis on weak topics","status":"completed"},{"content":"Week 3: Focus on Cardiovascular (10%) and GI (9%) with emphasis on weak topics","status":"completed"},{"content":"Week 4: Focus on Endocrine (8%) and Multisystem (8%) with emphasis on weak topics","status":"completed"},{"content":"Add targeted practice s