### 🚀 What This Skill Does

The **PDF Generation Skill** allows you to create professional PDF documents from markdown content with:

**Key Features:**
- **Professional formatting** with clean typography
- **Customizable output** for different document types
- **Automatic table of contents** for multi-section documents
- **Responsive formatting** for various content types

**Perfect for creating:**
- Study guides and handouts
- Clinical documentation templates  
- Educational materials
- Professional reports
- Revision notes

### 📋 How to Use It

1. **Prepare Content**: Structure your content with markdown headings (`##`, `###`), bullet points, and bold text
2. **Generate PDF**: Use the `generate_document` tool with format="pdf"
3. **Deliver**: Share the download link with your audience

### 💡 Example Workflow

```markdown
## My Study Guide
### Section 1
- Key point 1
- **Important concept**

### Section 2  
1. First step
2. Second step
```

The skill automatically formats this into a professional PDF with proper styling and structure.

### 🎯 Ready to Use

The PDF generation skill is now available in your skills library! When you need to create polished PDF documents for medical education or clinical purposes, just reference this skill and follow the workflow outlined in the instructions.

Would you like me to demonstrate by creating a sample PDF document using this skill?','[{"id":"call_0421767413ba4ad5a0cfda53","name":"write_todos","args":{"todos":[{"content":"Create pdf-generation skill directory structure","status":"pending"},{"content":"Create SKILL.md file with PDF generation instructions","status":"pending"},{"content":"Create supporting files for PDF generation","status":"pending"}]}},{"id":"call_fbd0e8416c804e808c434e1b","name":"write_todos","args":{"todos":[{"content":"Create pdf-generation skill directory structure","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Create SKILL.md file with PDF generation instructions","status":"pending"},{"content":"Create supporting files for PDF generation","status":"pending"}]}},{"id":"call_eff1390ad39b40b1b470cbb3","name":"mkdir","args":{"path":"/skills/pdf-generation"}},{"id":"call_3d749cec96364b3c90825adf","name":"write_file","args":{"content":"# PDF Generation Skill\\n\\nGenerate professional PDF documents from markdown content with customizable formatting options for medical education materials, study guides, and clinical documentation.\\n\\n## When to Use This Skill\\n\\nUse this skill when you need to create polished, downloadable PDF documents for:\\n- Study guides and handouts\\n- Clinical documentation templates\\n- Educational materials\\n- Professional reports\\n- Revision notes\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n### Step 1: Prepare Content Structure\\n- Organize content with clear markdown headings (`##`, `###`)\\n- Use bullet points (`-`) and numbered lists (`1.`, `2.`) for readability\\n- Include tables when comparing information\\n- Add bold text (`**key terms**`) for emphasis\\n\\n### Step 2: Generate PDF Document\\nUse the `generate_document` tool with these parameters:\\n- `title`: Human-friendly document title\\n- `content`: Full markdown content\\n- `format`: \\"pdf\\" (required for PDF output)\\n- `filename`: Optional custom filename (defaults to title-based)\\n\\n### Step 3: Review and Deliver\\n- The tool returns a preview and download link\\n- Documents are automatically formatted with professional styling\\n- Include the download link in your response\\n\\n## Content Guidelines\\n\\n### Markdown Structure Examples\\n```markdown\\n# Title (use ## for main heading)\\n\\n## Section 1\\n- Key point 1\\n- Key point 2\\n- **Important concept**\\n\\n## Section 2\\n1. First step\\n2. Second step\\n3. Third step\\n\\n## Comparison Table\\n| Feature | Option A | Option B |\\n|---------|----------|----------|\\n| Cost    | $100     | $150     |\\n| Time    | 2 weeks  | 1 week   |\\n\\n## Clinical Pearls\\n- **Pearl 1**: Remember to check X\\n- **Pearl 2**: Always consider Y\\n```\\n\\n### Best Practices\\n- Keep content concise but comprehensive\\n- Use clear section headings\\n- Include clinical pearls or key takeaways\\n- Format for easy reading (white space, bullet points)\\n- Include references when appropriate\\n\\n## Example Use Cases\\n\\n### Study Guide Creation\\n```markdown\\n## Cardiology Study Guide\\n\\n### Heart Failure\\n- **Definition**: Inability of heart to pump sufficient blood\\n- **Types**: HFrEF, HFpEF, HFmrEF\\n- **Treatment**: ACE inhibitors, beta-blockers, diuretics\\n\\n### ECG Interpretation\\n1. Rate assessment\\n2. Rhythm analysis\\n3. Axis determination\\n4. Morphology evaluation\\n```\\n\\n### Clinical Template\\n```markdown\\n## Patient Assessment Template\\n\\n### History\\n- **Chief Complaint**: [description]\\n- **History of Present Illness**: [details]\\n- **Past Medical History**: [relevant conditions]\\n\\n### Physical Examination\\n- **Vital Signs**: [values]\\n- **Cardiovascular**: [findings]\\n- **Respiratory**: [findings]\\n```\\n\\n## Output Format\\n- Professional PDF with clean typography\\n- Automatic table of contents for multi-section documents\\n- Responsive formatting for different content types\\n- Downloadable link provided to user\\n\\n## Troubleshooting\\n- Ensure markdown syntax is correct\\n- Check that all required para