tient history or context to make the rhythm recognition clinically applicable.\\n- The comparison table must fit on one page and highlight the most critical features that differentiate the rhythms.\\n- Feedback on the user''s answer should be constructive, explaining why their answer was correct or incorrect, and referencing specific ECG criteria.\\n- The scoring summary should show: total questions attempted, total points earned, percentage correct, and breakdown of points by category (rhythm identification only vs. rhythm + pathology/complication).\\n- The misses table should include columns for: Question Number, Your Answer, Correct Answer, Key Feature You Missed, and Clinical Significance of the Confused Rhythm.\\n- The final document should be saved as an artifact for the user''s review."}},{"id":"call_-7142158600360687449","name":"manage_skills","args":{"action":"improve","name":"ecg-rhythm-drill","description":"Drills the user on ECG rhythm recognition by presenting clinical vignettes with rhythm findings, checking their answers, and reinforcing with comparison tables of look-alike rhythms. Includes scoring rubric and summary of misses.","body":"---\\nname: ecg-rhythm-drill\\ndescription: \\"Drills the user on ECG rhythm recognition by presenting clinical vignettes with rhythm findings, checking their answers, and reinforcing with comparison tables of look-alike rhythms. Includes scoring rubric and summary of misses.\\"\\n---\\n\\n# ECG Rhythm Drill\\n\\n## When to use\\nThe user requests practice with ECG rhythm recognition, specifically asking for clinical vignettes with rhythm findings, answer checking, and reinforcement through comparison tables of similar rhythms.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n1. Use `search_medical_images` to find a relevant ECG image for the rhythm being tested, ensuring it''s clear and labeled.\\n2. Present a clinical vignette that includes the ECG findings and asks the user to identify the rhythm.\\n3. Once the user provides their answer, use `search_medical_references` to verify the correct rhythm and gather key distinguishing features.\\n4. Create a compact comparison table using `create_spreadsheet` that lists the correct rhythm and 2-3 common look-alike rhythms, with columns for: Rhythm Name, Key ECG Features, Clinical Significance, and Differentiating Tips.\\n5. Track the user''s performance ...[TRUNCATED]','[{"toolCallId":"call_-7142162998407196025","toolName":"read_file","content":"","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142159837311266080","toolName":"edit_file","content":"Error: permission denied for write on /skills/ecg-rhythm-drill/SKILL.md","isError":true},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142154030515481249","toolName":"write_file","content":"Error: permission denied for write on /skills/ecg-rhythm-drill-improved/SKILL.md","isError":true},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142158600360687449","toolName":"manage_skills","content":"{\\"ok\\":true,\\"improved\\":true,\\"skillId\\":\\"cmvmlhazp0001q1rdiwnujefr\\",\\"name\\":\\"ecg-rhythm-drill\\",\\"revisionCount\\":1,\\"note\\":\\"the improved version loads on the next turn; the previous one is restorable from history\\"}","isError":false}]',NULL,'2026-10-24T17:25:33.055Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvmo9dc7000dwgrdsvsabjhy','345fa648-ce40-4976-9998-3d93affdcdb9','user','Quick test — use your ecg-rhythm-drill skill and give me exactly ONE practice vignette, then stop.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-24T17:27:46.375Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvmo9pq0000hwgrdl9v0vmi6','345fa648-ce40-4976-9998-3d93affdcdb9','assistant','I''ll use the ECG rhythm drill skill to give you one practice vignette.

Here''s your ECG rhythm drill practice vignette:

---

**ECG Rhythm Drill - Practice Vignette**

**Clinical Vignette:**
A 72-year-old male with a history of hypertension and heart failure presents to the emergency department with palpitations and shortness of breath. He reports feeling his heart "beating irregularly" for the past 2 hours. Vital signs show a blood pressure of 142/88 mmHg, respiratory rate of 18/min, and oxygen saturation of 98% on room air. An ECG is obtained (shown below).

**ECG Findings:**
![ECG showing atrial fibrillation with irregularly irregular rhythm](/generated/imgcache/eb1ba87f3a1bfccb.jpg)

**Question:** What is the rhythm shown in this ECG, and what are the key ECG features that support your diagnosis?

**Please identify the rhythm and provide your answer.**

---

*Reference: [S1] Atrial fibrillation is characterized by an irregularly irregular ventricular rhythm with absent discrete P waves and variable fibrillatory activity [S2] Key diagnostic criteria include no P waves, irregularly irregular rhythm, and QRS complexes usually < 120ms.*','[{"id":"call_-7142162689169549411","name":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/skills/ecg-rhythm-drill/SKILL.md","limit":1000}},{"id":"call_-7142157638288007821","name":"search_medical_images","args":{"query":"ECG atrial fibrillation rhythm strip","count":1}},{"id":"call_-7142161246060540345","name":"search_medical_references","args":{"query":"ECG atrial fibrillation diagnostic criteria irregular irregularly irregular","maxResults":3}}]','[{"toolCallId":"call_-7142162689169549411","toolName":"read_file","content":"","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142157638288007821","toolName":"search_medical_images","content":"{\\"found\\":true,\\"query\\":\\"ECG atrial fibrillation rhythm strip\\",\\"images\\":[{\\"index\\":1,\\"imageUrl\\":\\"/generated/imgcache/eb1ba87f3a1bfccb.jpg\\",\\"caption\\":\\"An ECG chart showing irregular heart rhythms with red text \\\\\\"ATRIAL FIBRILLATION\\\\\\" over dark blue gradient background.\\",\\"source\\":\\"YouTube\\",\\"dimensions\\":\\"1280pxx720px\\",\\"sourceUrl\\":\\"https://z-cdn.chatglm.cn/image-search-mcp/images-ppt/66e0405211d8.jpg\\",\\"cached\\":true}],\\"note\\":\\"Show the most relevant images inline with their sources. Each imageUrl is a LOCAL copy that always loads — embed it directly as ![caption](imageUrl) and name the original source site next to it. sourceUrl (when present) is the original remote image for attribution; only embed sourceUrl if imageUrl somehow fails.\\"}","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142161246060540345","toolName":"search_medical_references","content":"{\\"results\\":[{\\"title\\":\\"Atrial Fibrillation - StatPearls - NCBI Bookshelf - NIH\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK526072\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Sep 3, 2026 — A typical ECG demonstrates an irregularly irregular ventricular rhythm with absent discrete P waves and variable fibrillatory activity.\\",\\"host\\":\\"www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\\",\\"date\\":\\"Sep 3, 2026\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Atrial Fibrillation - ECG Library Diagnosis\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://litfl.com/atrial-fibrillation-ecg-library\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"by C calculator via MDCalc — ECG Features of Atrial Fibrillation Irregularly irregular rhythm No P waves. S complexes usually < 120ms, Irregularly irregular ventricular rate\\",\\"host\\":\\"litfl.com\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"Atrial Fibrillation: Knowing the Basics\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://clinicalview.gehealthcare.com/white-paper/atrial-fibrillation-knowing-basics\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"by ECG General — ECG showing atrial fibrillation Atrial fibrillation: “irregularly irregular” ventricular rhythm with an absence of P waves and often irregular waves in the ... Read more\\",\\"host\\":\\"clinicalview.gehealthcare.com\\",\\"date\\":\\"\\"}],\\"formatted\\":\\"[S1] Atrial Fibrillation - StatPearls - NCBI Bookshelf - NIH (Sep 3, 2026)\\\\n    https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK526072 (www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov)\\\\n    Sep 3, 2026 — A typical ECG demonstrates an irregularly irregular ventricular rhythm with absent discrete P waves and variable fibrillatory activity.\\\\n[S2] Atrial Fibrillation - ECG Library Diagnosis\\\\n    https://litfl.com/atrial-fibrillation-ecg-library (litfl.com)\\\\n    by C calculator via MDCalc — ECG Features of Atrial Fibrillation Irregularly irregular rhythm No P waves. S complexes usually < 120ms, Irregularly irregular ventricular rate\\\\n[S3] Atrial Fibrillation: Knowing the Basics\\\\n    https://clinicalview.gehealthcare.com/white-paper/atrial-fibrillation-knowing-basics (clinicalview.gehealthcare.com)\\\\n    by ECG General — ECG showing atrial fibrillation Atrial fibrillation: “irregularly irregular” ventricular rhythm with an absence of P waves and often irregular waves in the ... Read more\\",\\"note\\":\\"Cite these inline as [S1], [S2]… markers placed right after the claim each source supports. NEVER paste raw URLs into the answer text — the interface renders [S#] markers as clickable source cards and lists every URL in a Web sources panel automatically. Results are re-ranked for recency (freshest first): when a source carries a date, mention the year the moment you cite it (e.g. \\\\\\"per the 2024 ESC guideline [S1]\\\\\\"), and prefer the most recent guidance when sources conflict — flag older sources as superseded where relevant.\\"}","isError":false}]',NULL,'2026-10-24T17:28:02.424Z');
