INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvms3jll000wudrdbzjhm7wc','767ccda4-6f99-435d-b358-f5dd72eda290','assistant','Perfect! Now I''ll create a personalized 6-week study plan for your USMLE Step 1 exam, focusing on strengthening your cardiovascular physiology and pharmacology areas.

## 🎯 Your Personalized 6-Week USMLE Step 1 Study Plan

Based on your exam details and performance data, here''s your customized study plan:

### 📊 **Your Performance Overview**
- **Overall accuracy**: 36% (11 total attempts)
- **Weakest topics**: anemia (0/3 correct) and ACE inhibitors (0/2 correct)
- **Weakest systems**: General (0/5 correct) and Gastrointestinal (1/2 correct)

### 📈 **Exam Blueprint & Your 6-Week Allocation**

| Area | Exam Weight | Your Weeks | Focus Areas |
|------|-------------|------------|-------------|
| **Cardiovascular System** | 10% | **2 weeks** | ⭐ **Priority: Physiology & Pharmacology** |
| **Respiratory & Renal** | 17% | 1 week | High-weight area |
| **General Principles** | 14% | 1 week | Include anemia focus |
| **Behavioral Health & Neuro** | 13% | 1 week | |
| **Musculoskeletal & Skin** | 11% | 0.5 weeks | |
| **Blood & Immune** | 9% | 0.5 weeks | |
| **Gastrointestinal** | 9% | **1 week** | ⭐ **Priority: Your weak area** |
| **Endocrine** | 8% | Integrated | |
| **Reproductive** | 7% | Integrated | |
| **Multisystem** | 8% | Final week | |

### 🗓️ **Weekly Breakdown**

**Week 1: Cardiovascular Physiology Deep Dive**
- Cardiac cycle, ECG interpretation, hemodynamics
- Heart failure pathophysiology and compensatory mechanisms
- **Target**: Build strong foundation for pharmacology

**Week 2: Cardiovascular Pharmacology + Anemia Focus**
- Antihypertensives (including ACE inhibitors - your weakest area)
- Antiarrhythmics, antianginals, lipid-lowering agents
- **Special focus**: Anemia classification and management

**Week 3: Respiratory & Renal Systems**
- Pulmonary physiology, acid-base balance
- Renal physiology, electrolyte disorders

**Week 4: General Principles + Gastrointestinal**
- Biochemistry, cell biology, genetics
- **GI focus**: Your 50% accuracy area needs reinforcement

**Week 5: Behavioral Health & Musculoskeletal**
- Neurophysiology, psychopathology
- Bone/joint disorders, skin conditions

**Week 6: Integrated Review & Practice**
- Multisystem processes
- Full-length practice exams
- Weak area reinforcement

### 🎯 **Immediate Action Items**

