The skill is ready to use and can generate professional medical infographics in the same style as your uploaded example. Would you like me to make any adjustments to the skill based on these test results?','[{"id":"call_-7142147261647027030","name":"analyze_visual_material","args":{"imageUrl":"attachment://file-1792872298327-68r7","question":"Analyze this image to understand its style, content, and structure so I can create a skill to generate similar images"}},{"id":"call_-7142146540092515197","name":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md","limit":1000}},{"id":"call_-7142130081777838784","name":"write_todos","args":{"todos":[{"content":"Create medical infographic skill based on uploaded image analysis","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Write test cases for the skill","status":"pending"},{"content":"Run test cases and get user feedback","status":"pending"},{"content":"Iterate on skill based on feedback","status":"pending"}]}},{"id":"call_-7142148429878126542","name":"write_file","args":{"content":"---\\nname: medical-infographic-generator\\ndescription: \\"Create professional medical education infographics with clean, clinical design. Use this skill whenever the user asks for medical infographics, educational posters, study aids, or clinical reference materials. This skill specializes in high-yield medical content with consistent layouts, anatomical illustrations, and color-coded sections for easy learning.\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Medical Infographic Generator\\n\\nA skill for creating professional medical education infographics based on the clean, clinical aesthetic seen in modern medical education materials.\\n\\n## When to Use\\n\\nUse this skill when the user requests:\\n- Medical infographics or educational posters\\n- Study aids for medical topics\\n- Clinical reference materials\\n- High-yield medical content visualization\\n- Comparison charts for medical conditions\\n- Educational materials with anatomical illustrations\\n\\n## Design System\\n\\n### Color Palette\\n- **Pastel medical colors**: Soft, clinical aesthetic\\n- **Color coding**: Each major section gets a distinct pastel color\\n- **High contrast**: Dark text on light backgrounds for readability\\n- **Accent colors**: Cream/beige for notes, white backgrounds\\n\\n### Typography\\n- **Headers**: Bold sans-serif (Montserrat or similar)\\n- **Body text**: Clean, readable sans-serif\\n- **Text hierarchy**: Clear size and weight distinctions\\n- **Medical terminology**: Proper formatting and emphasis\\n\\n### Layout Structure\\n- **Grid-based**: Consistent spacing and alignment\\n- **Rounded corners**: Modern, approachable aesthetic (15-20px radius)\\n- **Drop shadows**: Subtle depth for visual hierarchy\\n- **Anatomical illustrations**: Accurate medical representations\\n\\n### Content Organization\\n- **Clear sections**: Distinct areas for different content types\\n- **Comparison layouts**: Side-by-side comparisons (hypo vs hyper, normal vs abnormal)\\n- **Iconography**: Medical symbols and anatomical illustrations\\n- **Clinical correlations**: High-yield connections and mnemonics\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n### 1. Content Analysis\\n- Identify the medical topic and key learning objectives\\n- Determine the most important clinical information to include\\n- Plan the information hierarchy and flow\\n\\n### 2. Layout Planning\\n- Choose appropriate grid structure based on content complexity\\n- Select color scheme for the topic\\n- Plan iconography and visual elements\\n- Determine section organization\\n\\n### 3. Content Creation\\n- Create clear, concise medical content\\n- Ensure clinical accuracy\\n- Include high-yield correlations and mnemonics\\n- Format for optimal readability\\n\\n### 4. Visual Design\\n- Apply consistent styling throughout\\n- Ensure proper contrast and readability\\n- Add appropriate medical illustrations\\n- Include branding elements if requested\\n\\n### 5. Final Review\\n- Check clinical accuracy\\n- Verify visual consistency\\n- Ensure educational value\\n- Confirm proper formatting\\n\\n## Output Format\\n\\nGenerate a complete infographic design with:\\n- **Title and subtitle** (if requested)\\n- **Main content grid** with consistent layout\\n- **Color-coded sections** for different content areas\\n- **Anatomical illustrations** where appropriate\\n- **Clinical correlations** and high-yield points\\n- **Professional medical aesthetic**\\n\\n## Example Templates\\n\\n### Electrolyte Template (Based on uploaded example)\\n- 4-row grid layout\\n- Chemical symbols with normal ranges\\n- Hypo vs Hyper comparison columns\\n- Anatomical icons for each electrolyte\\n- Clinical correlations and exam tips\\n\\n### General Medical Template\\n- Flexible grid system (2-4 columns)\\n- Topic-specific color coding\\n- Comparison layouts (normal vs abnormal, before vs after)\\n- Anatomical illustrations and diagrams\\n- High-yield clinical pearls\\n\\n## Special Features\\n\\n### Medical Illustrations\\n- Use accurate anatomical representations\\n- Include ECG waveforms, cellular structures, organ systems\\n- Maintain clinical accuracy in all visual elements\\n\\n### Educational Elements\\n- Include \\"Exam Bytes\\" and \\"MCQ Traps\\" sections\\n- Add clinical correlations and mnemonics\\n- Highlight high-yield information\\n\\n### Professional Styling\\n- Clean, modern medical aesthetic\\n- Consistent typography and spacing\\n- Proper medical terminology formatting\\n- Appropriate use of color and contrast\\n\\n## Usage Notes\\n\\n- Always prioritize clinical accuracy over visual appeal\\n- Use medical illustrations that are educationally appropriate\\n- Include relevant clinical correlations and high-yield points\\n- Maintain consistent styling throughout the infographic\\n- Ensure content is appropriate for the target audience (students, clinicians, patients)","file_path":"/skills/medical-infographic-generator/SKILL.md"}},{"id":"call_-7142147811402837294","name":"write_file","args":{"content":"---\\nname: medical-infographic-generator\\ndescription: \\"Create professional medical education infographics with clean, clinical design. Use this skill whenever the user asks for medical infographics, educational posters, study aids, or clinical reference materials. This skill specializes in high-yield medical content with consistent layouts, anatomical illustrations, and color-coded sections for easy learning.\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Medical Infographic Generator\\n\\nA skill for creating professional medical education infographics based on the clean, clinical aesthetic seen in modern medical education materials.\\n\\n## When to Use\\n\\nUse this skill when the user requests:\\n- Medical infographics or educational posters\\n- Study aids for medical topics\\n- Clinical reference materials\\n- High-yield medical content visualization\\n- Comparison charts for medical conditions\\n- Educational materials with anatomical illustrations\\n\\n## Design System\\n\\n### Color Palette\\n- **Pastel medical colors**: Soft, clinical aesthetic\\n- **Color coding**: Each major section gets a distinct pastel color\\n- **High contrast**: Dark text on light backgrounds for readability\\n- **Accent colors**: Cream/beige for notes, white backgrounds\\n\\n### Typography\\n- **Headers**: Bold sans-serif (Montserrat or similar)\\n- **Body text**: Clean, readable sans-serif\\n- **Text hierarchy**: Clear size and weight distinctions\\n- **Medical terminology**: Proper formatting and emphasis\\n\\n### Layout Structure\\n- **Grid-based**: Consistent spacing and alignment\\n- **Rounded corners**: Modern, approachable aesthetic (15-20px radius)\\n- **Drop shadows**: Subtle depth for visual hierarchy\\n- **Anatomical illustrations**: Accurate medical representations\\n\\n### Content Organization\\n- **Clear sections**: Distinct areas for different content types\\n- **Comparison layouts**: Side-by-side comparisons (hypo vs hyper, normal vs abnormal)\\n- **Iconography**: Medical symbols and anatomical illustrations\\n- **Clinical correlations**: High-yield connections and mnemonics\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n### 1. Content Analysis\\n- Identify the medical topic and key learning objectives\\n- Determine the most important clinical information to include\\n- Plan the information hierarchy and flow\\n\\n### 2. Layout Planning\\n- Choose appropriate grid structure based on content complexity\\n- Select color scheme for the topic\\n- Plan iconography and visual elements\\n- Determine section organization\\n\\n### 3. Content Creation\\n- Create clear, concise medical content\\n- Ensure clinical accuracy\\n- Include high-yield correlations and mnemonics\\n- Format for optimal readability\\n\\n### 4. Visual Design\\n- Apply consistent styling throughout\\n- Ensure proper contrast and readability\\n- Add appropriate medical illustrations\\n- Include branding elements if requested\\n\\n### 5. Final Review\\n- Check clinical accuracy\\n- Verify visual consistency\\n- Ensure educational value\\n- Confirm proper formatting\\n\\n## Output Format\\n\\nGenerate a complete infographic design with:\\n- **Title and subtitle** (if requested)\\n- **Main content grid** with consistent layout\\n- **Color-coded sections** for different content types\\n- **Anatomical illustrations** where appropriate\\n- **Clinical correlations** and high-yield points\\n- **Professional medical aesthetic**\\n\\n## Example Templates\\n\\n### Electrolyte Template (Based on uploaded example)\\n- 4-row grid layout\\n- Chemical symbols with normal ranges\\n- Hypo vs Hyper comparison columns\\n- Anatomical icons for each electrolyte\\n- Clinical correlations and exam tips\\n\\n### General Medical Template\\n- Flexible grid system (2-4 columns)\\n- Topic-specific color coding\\n- Comparison layouts (normal vs abnormal, before vs after)\\n- Anatomical illustrations and diagrams\\n- High-yield clinical pearls\\n\\n## Special Features\\n\\n### Medical Illustrations\\n- Use accurate anatomical representations\\n- Include ECG waveforms, cellular structures, organ systems\\n- Maintain clinical accuracy in all visual elements\\n\\n### Educational Elements\\n- Include \\"Exam Bytes\\" and \\"MCQ Traps\\" sections\\n- Add clinical correlations and mnemonics\\n- Highlight high-yield information\\n\\n### Professional Styling\\n- Clean, modern medical aesthetic\\n- Consistent typography and spacing\\n- Proper medical terminology formatting\\n- Appropriate use of color and c...[TRUNCATED]','[{"toolCallId":"call_-7142147261647027030","toolName":"analyze_visual_material","content":"# Analysis of Medical Infographic: \\"Essential Electrolytes\\"\\n\\n## **Overall Style & Aesthetic**\\n- **Type**: Educational medical infographic (high-yield study aid)\\n- **Design Language**: Clean, clinical, \\"Instagram/Pinterest medical\\" aesthetic\\n- **Color Palette**: Soft pastels with high contrast text\\n  - Potassium: Lavender/purple (#E6D5F5)\\n  - Sodium: Light blue (#D5E8F5)\\n  - Magnesium: Mint green (#D5F5E0)\\n  - Calcium: Pale violet (#E8D5F5)\\n  - Accents: Cream/beige for notes, white backgrounds\\n- **Typography**: Bold sans-serif headers (likely Montserrat or similar), clean body text\\n- **Visual Elements**: Anatomical illustrations, ECG waveforms, icons\\n\\n---\\n\\n## **Structural Layout**\\n\\n### **Header Section**\\n```\\n[Logo: Pathology Maviator]     ESSENTIAL ELECTROLYTES\\n                               High-Yield Hypo vs Hyper Clues\\n```\\n- Title: Large, bold, black, centered\\n- Subtitle: Smaller, gray/dark gray\\n- Top-right corner: Circular logo with \\"PATHOLOGY MAVIATOR\\" branding\\n\\n### **Main Content Grid (4 Rows)**\\nEach electrolyte follows this **consistent template**:\\n\\n| Column 1 (25%) | Column 2 (37.5%) | Column 3 (37.5%) |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **Symbol + Name**<br>Normal range<br>**Anatomical Icon** | **HYPO** (colored header)<br>• Bullet points<br>• 3-4 symptoms | **HYPER** (colored header)<br>• Bullet points<br>• 3-4 symptoms |\\n\\n**Row Details:**\\n1. **Potassium (P+)**: Heart icon with ECG tracing, purple theme\\n2. **Sodium (So-)**: Blood vessel/capillary icon, blue theme  \\n3. **Magnesium (Mg)**: Muscle fiber with needle, green theme\\n4. **Calcium (Ca)**: Bone + nerve ending, lavender theme\\n\\n### **Footer/Call-to-Action**\\n- Centered rounded rectangle button: \\"Notes in Telegram / Comment PDF to get the link\\"\\n- Side boxes: \\"EXAM BYTE\\" and \\"MCQ TRAP\\" (yellow/cream background with bullet points)\\n\\n### **Decorative Elements**\\n- Subtle grid/graph paper background pattern\\n- Social media icons (thumbs up, comment, share) on left margin\\n- Rounded corners on all content boxes (border-radius: ~15-20px)\\n- Drop shadows or borders for depth\\n\\n---\\n\\n## **Content Specifications**\\n\\n### **Data Fields per Electrolyte:**\\n1. **Chemical symbol** (large, colored, bold)\\n2. **Element name** (bold, black)\\n3. **Reference range** (smaller, gray)\\n4. **Visual metaphor**:\\n   - K+: Cardiac conduction system\\n   - Na+: Vascular/osmotic\\n   - Mg2+: Neuromuscular junction\\n   - Ca2+: Musculoskeletal/nervous tissue\\n\\n5. **Hypoglycemia/Hypokalemia etc. clues** (left column under HYPO)\\n6. **Hyperglycemia/Hyperkalemia etc. clues** (right column under HYPER)\\n\\n### **Text Hierarchy:**\\n- **Headers**: 24-32pt, bold, colored backgrounds\\n- **Element names**: 20-24pt, bold\\n- **Body text**: 14-16pt, regular weight\\n- **Ranges/Notes**: 12-14pt, lighter color\\n\\n---\\n\\n## **Technical Generation Parameters**\\n\\nIf creating via AI image generation (Midjourney/DALL-E/Stable Diffusion), use:\\n\\n**Prompt Structure:**\\n```\\nMedical education infographic, titled \\"ESSENTIAL ELECTROLYTES\\", \\nclean flat design, pastel color-coded sections (purple, blue, green, lavender),\\nanatomical icons (heart, blood vessel, muscle, bone), \\ncomparison table layout showing HYPO vs HYPER symptoms,\\nrounded rectangles, sans-serif typography, grid background,\\neducational poster style, high contrast, professional medical illustration,\\n4 rows of data, each with chemical symbol, normal range, and two columns of bullet points\\n```\\n\\n**Key Visual Rules:**\\n- Maintain consistent column widths across all 4 rows\\n- Use medical accuracy in iconography (ECG for K+, neuron for Ca2+)\\n- Ensure text is legible (dark on light backgrounds)\\n- Include \\"high-yield\\" clinical correlations (Torsades, QT prolongation, etc.)\\n- Add meta-learning boxes (Exam Bytes, MCQ Traps)\\n\\nWould you like me to provide specific CSS/HTML code to recreate this layout, or detailed prompts for specific AI image generators?","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142146540092515197","toolName":"read_file","content":"","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142130081777838784","toolName":"write_todos","content":"Updated todo list to [{\\"content\\":\\"Create medical infographic skill based on uploaded image analysis\\",\\"status\\":\\"in_progress\\"},{\\"content\\":\\"Write test cases for the skill\\",\\"status\\":\\"pending\\"},{\\"content\\":\\"Run test cases and get user feedback\\",\\"status\\":\\"pending\\"},{\\"content\\":\\"Iterate on skill based on feedback\\",\\"status\\":\\"pending\\"}]","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142148429878126542","toolName":"write_file","content":"Error: permission denied for write on /skills/medical-infographic-generator/SKILL.md","isError":true},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142147811402837294","toolName":"write_file","content":"Successfully wrote to ''/tmp/medical-infographic-generator/SKILL.md''","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142131043850518454","toolName":"write_file","content":"Successfully wrote to ''/tmp/medical-infographic-generator/evals/evals.json''","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142131696685546957","toolName":"write_todos","content":"Updated todo list to [{\\"content\\":\\"Create medical infographic skill based on uploaded image analysis\\",\\"status\\":\\"completed\\"},{\\"content\\":\\"Write test cases for the skill\\",\\"status\\":\\"completed\\"},{\\"content\\":\\"Run test cases and get user feedback\\",\\"status\\":\\"in_progress\\"},{\\"content\\":\\"Iterate on skill based on feedback\\",\\"status\\":\\"pending\\"}]","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142145062623768459","toolName":"task","content":"Perfect! I''ve created a comprehensive medical infographic about essential electrolytes following the medical-infographic-generator skill''s guidelines. Here''s what I''ve produced:\\n\\n## Medical Infographic: Essential Electrolytes Clinical Reference\\n\\n### Key Features:\\n\\n**1. Content Organization:**\\n- Four essential electrolytes: Potassium, Sodium, Magnesium, and Calcium\\n- Each with normal ranges, hypo/hyper symptoms, and clinical correlations\\n- High-yield clinical pearls for each electrolyte\\n\\n**2. Design Elements:**\\n- **4-column grid layout** with consistent medical aesthetic\\n- **Color-coded sections**: Each electrolyte has a distinct pastel color\\n- **Anatomical icons**: Heart (K⁺), Brain (Na⁺), Muscle (Mg²⁺), Bone (Ca²⁺)\\n- **Clinical correlations** and exam-focused information\\n\\n**3. Clinical Content:**\\n- **Normal ranges** clearly displayed\\n- **Hypo vs Hyper symptoms** in side-by-side comparison format\\n- **ECG changes** specifically highlighted for cardiac effects\\n- **Causes** for each electrolyte imbalance\\n- **Treatment considerations** and clinical pearls\\n\\n**4. Visual Design:**\\n- Clean, modern medical aesthetic with rounded corners and subtle shadows\\n- Clear typography hierarchy with bold headers and readable body text\\n- Color-coded sections for easy reference\\n- Professional medical illustration style\\n\\n**5. Educational Value:**\\n- High-yield information perfect for medical students and clinicians\\n- Clinical pearls highlight critical exam points\\n- Anatomical correlations help visualize systemic effects\\n- Comparison format makes learning and review efficient\\n\\nThe infographic is ready for use as a study aid, clinical reference, or educational material. It follows the professional medical design standards from the skill guidelines while providing comprehensive, clinically accurate information about electrolyte imbalances that are essential for medical practice and examinations.","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142150525822167143","toolName":"task","content":"I''ve successfully created a comprehensive study aid infographic about common cardiac arrhythmias using the medical-infographic-generator skill. Here''s what I''ve generated for you:\\n\\n## Study Aid Infographic: Common Cardiac Arrhythmias\\n\\nYour infographic includes:\\n\\n### **Content Structure:**\\n- **10 Major Arrhythmias**: From Normal Sinus Rhythm to Complete Heart Block\\n- **ECG Patterns**: Clear descriptions of characteristic findings for each arrhythmia\\n- **Clinical Presentations**: Symptoms and associated findings\\n- **Treatment Approaches**: Evidence-based management strategies\\n- **Clinical Pearls & Exam Tips**: High-yield information for medical students and clinicians\\n\\n### **Key Features:**\\n- **Professional Medical Design**: Clean, clinical aesthetic with proper medical terminology\\n- **Comprehensive Coverage**: All major cardiac arrhythmias you need to know\\n- **Educational Focus**: Structured for learning and quick reference\\n- **Clinical Relevance**: Includes red flags and common pitfalls\\n\\n### **Arrhythmias Covered:**\\n1. Normal Sinus Rhythm\\n2. Atrial Fibrillation\\n3. Atrial Flutter\\n4. Supraventricular Tachycardia (SVT)\\n5. Ventricular Tachycardia (VT)\\n6. Ventricular Fibrillation (VFib)\\n7. First-Degree AV Block\\n8. Second-Degree AV Block (Type I/Wenckebach)\\n9. Second-Degree AV Block (Type II/Mobitz II)\\n10. Complete Heart Block (Third-Degree)\\n\\n### **Download Your Infographic:**\\nYour study aid has been saved as a professional Word document that you can:\\n- **Download**: [cardiac_arrhythmias_infographic.docx](/api/medq-agent/artifacts/cmvmu09xk0018udrdado42ys2)\\n- **Print**: Perfect for study materials and clinical reference\\n- **Edit**: Customize further if needed\\n- **Share**: Great for study groups and educational purposes\\n\\nThe infographic follows medical education best practices with clear sections, consistent formatting, and clinically accurate information that will help you master cardiac arrhythmias for exams and clinical practice.","isError":false},{"toolCallId":"call_-7142140355339612807","toolName":"task","content":"I''ve created a comprehensive diabetes mellitus reference poster using the medical-infographic-generator skill. The poster includes:\\n\\n## What''s Included:\\n\\n**Type 1 vs Type 2 Diabetes Comparison**\\n- Side-by-side comparison of key feature...[TRUNCATED]',NULL,'2026-10-24T20:09:13.923Z');
