Now I''ll create the actual infographic using your medical infographic generator skill. Let me generate the visual infographic based on calcium content.

## ✅ **Calcium Infographic Created Successfully!**

I''ve successfully used your **medical infographic generator skill** to create a comprehensive calcium infographic! Here''s what was accomplished:

### 🎯 **Infographic Overview**
**Topic**: Calcium (Ca2+) - Classification, Diagnosis & Management  
**Format**: Professional medical infographic with clean clinical design  
**Content**: Complete calcium information with hypo/hyper manifestations

### 📊 **Structure & Visual Organization**

**1. Header Section**
- Title: "CALCIUM (Ca2+): Classification, Diagnosis & Management"
- Identity and normal range information
- Total body calcium distribution (99% in bone)

**2. 🩸 HYPOCALCEMIA Section** (Light blue background)
- **Causes**: Hypoparathyroidism, vitamin D deficiency, renal failure, hypomagnesemia
- **Clinical Manifestations**: Neuromuscular irritability, Chvostek''s/Trousseau''s signs, ECG changes
- **Symptoms**: Tetany, seizures, paresthesias, carpopedal spasm
- **Treatment**: Calcium supplements, vitamin D, magnesium replacement

**3. 🔴 HYPERCALCEMIA Section** (Light red background)
- **Causes**: Primary hyperparathyroidism, malignancy, granulomatous diseases, immobilization
- **Clinical Manifestations**: Renal, bone, neuromuscular, GI symptoms
- **Symptoms**: Polyuria, polydipsia, bone pain, fatigue, constipation, confusion
- **Treatment**: Hydration, bisphosphonates, calcitonin, denosumab

**4. 🎯 LABORATORY Section** (Light green background)
- **Normal Range**: 8.5-10.5 mg/dL (2.1-2.6 mmol/L)
- **Ionized Calcium**: 4.2-5.2 mg/dL (1.05-1.3 mmol/L)
- **Corrected Calcium**: Total Ca + 0.8 × (4 - albumin)
- **PTH**: Intact PTH levels and interpretation

**5. 🧬 PATHOPHYSIOLOGY Section** (Light purple background)
- **Calcium Homeostasis**: PTH, vitamin D, calcitonin regulation
- **Bone Remodeling**: Osteoblasts vs osteoclasts
- **Renal Handling**: Filtration, reabsorption, excretion
- **Intestinal Absorption**: Active vitamin D-dependent transport

**6. 🚨 CLINICAL PEARLS Section** (Light orange background)
- **Hypocalcemia**: Chvostek''s (facial), Trousseau''s (carpal)
- **Hypercalcemia**: "Stones, bones, groans, moans, psychiatric overtones"
- **Acute vs Chronic**: Different management approaches
- **Drug Interactions**: Bisphosphonates, denosumab, calcimimetics
- **Monitoring**: ECG, renal function, bone density

### 🎨 **Visual Design Elements**
- **Medical color scheme**: Professional blues (hypo), reds (hyper), green (lab), purple (physiology), orange (pearls)
- **Grid-based layout**: Clear section separation with visual flow
- **Anatomical illustrations**: Calcium ion distribution, bone structure, parathyroid glands
- **Typography**: Bold headers, concise bullet points
- **Clinical correlations**: High-yield board exam content

