INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvogchq7000pspwub1b3g5au','cb3d48a8-c2aa-4bb9-9f96-45bdd224be0a','user','What are the current ESC 2024 guidelines on hypertension thresholds? Cite your sources.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-25T23:21:47.455Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvogderz000xspwusffkiaip','cb3d48a8-c2aa-4bb9-9f96-45bdd224be0a','assistant','I''ll search for the current ESC 2024 guidelines on hypertension thresholds for you.

Let me get more detailed information from the official ESC guideline document:

Let me try to access the actual guideline document more directly:

Let me get more detailed information from the Medscape article which appears to have the most comprehensive coverage:

Let me try a more specific search to find the actual guideline content:

Let me get the detailed information from the PMC article which appears to have comprehensive coverage:

Based on my search of current medical literature and guidelines, here are the key hypertension threshold changes in the 2024 ESC guidelines:

## Current ESC 2024 Hypertension Thresholds

The 2024 ESC guidelines introduced a **new three-category classification system** for blood pressure [S1, S2]:

### 1. **Non-elevated Blood Pressure**
- **Office BP <120/70 mmHg**
- Drug treatment is **not recommended** [S2]

### 2. **Elevated Blood Pressure** (NEW CATEGORY)
- **Office systolic BP 120–139 mmHg OR diastolic BP 70–89 mmHg**
- Drug treatment is **recommended based on cardiovascular disease risk and follow-up BP level** [S1, S2, S4]
- This is a new category added in 2024 to capture individuals who may benefit from early intervention [S4]

### 3. **Hypertension**
- **Office BP ≥140/90 mmHg**
- **Prompt confirmation and drug treatment is recommended in all individuals** [S2]

## Key Changes from Previous Guidelines

1. **New "Elevated" Category**: The 2024 guidelines added the elevated category (120-139/70-89 mmHg) which didn''t exist in previous classifications [S1, S4]

2. **Lower Threshold for Non-elevated**: Previously, normal/non-hypertensive started at 130/80 mmHg; now it''s <120/70 mmHg [S2]

3. **Treatment Targets**: 
   - Initial default systolic BP treatment target is **120–129 mmHg** for most patients
   - **Relaxed targets** (BP as low as reasonably achievable) are recommended in cases of:
     - Treatment intolerance
     - Adults ≥85 years
     - Symptomatic orthostasis
     - Moderate-to-severe frailty
     - Limited life expectancy [S2]

## Sources:
- [S1] Management of Elevated Blood Pressure and Hypertension - Medscape (Mar 12, 2025)
- [S2] What''s New and Different in the 2024 ESC Guideline - PMC (2024)
- [S4] 2024 ESC guideline for diagnosis of elevated BP and hypertension - Social media post

These guidelines represent a shift toward more aggressive early identification and management of elevated blood pressure, with the new "elevated" category allowing for earlier intervention based on cardiovascular risk assessment.','[{"id":"call_-7142064660835988852","name":"search_medical_references","args":{"query":"ESC 2024 hypertension guidelines thresholds blood pressure","maxResults":3}},{"id":"call_-7142057307851975941","name":"fetch_medical_reference","args":{"url":"https://www.escardio.org/guidelines/clinical-practice-guidelines/all-esc-practice-guidelines/elevated-blood-pressure-and-hypertension","maxChars":5000}},{"id":"call_-7142064660835988568","name":"search_medical_references","args":{"query":"\\"2024 ESC guidelines\\" hypertension \\"blood pressure thresholds\\" \\"elevated blood pressure\\"","maxResults":5}},{"id":"call_-7142057617089618463","name":"fetch_medical_reference","args":{"url":"https://reference.medscape.com","maxChars":8000}},{"id":"call_-7142055246267671599","name":"search_medical_references","args":{"query":"\\"elevated blood pressure\\" \\"120-139 mmHg\\" \\"70-89 mmHg\\" ESC 2024","maxResults":5}},{"id":"call_-7142058132485697172","name":"fetch_medical_reference","args":{"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12011322","maxChars":6000}}]','[{"toolCallId":"call_-7142064660835988852","toolName":"search_medical_references","content":"{\\"results\\":[{\\"title\\":\\"Hypertension and Blood Pressure Control: ESC 2024\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://reference.medscape.com\\",\\"snippet\\":\\"Nov 25, 2024 — Updated ESC guidance introduces a new category of elevated BP, defined as office systolic BP 120–139 mmHg or diastolic BP 70–89 mmHg … g or ...\\",\\"host\\":\\"reference.medscape.com\\",\\"date\\":\\"Nov 25, 2024\\"},{\\"title\\":\\"2024 Elevated Blood Pressure and Hypertension\\",\\"url\\":\\"https://www.escardio.org/guidelines/clinical-practice-guidelines/all-esc-practice-guidelines/elevated-blood-pressure-and-hypertension\\",\\"snippe