Opened the Question Bank for you.','[{"id":"call_-7142064008000961937","name":"ui_action","args":{"actions":[{"type":"navigate","target":"bank"}]}}]','[{"toolCallId":"call_-7142064008000961937","toolName":"ui_action","content":"{\\"dispatched\\":true,\\"count\\":1,\\"types\\":[\\"navigate\\"],\\"guidance\\":\\"The action(s) were dispatched to the learner''s screen and will execute live. In your final reply, say in one short sentence what you did (e.g. \\\\\\"Opened the Question Bank for you\\\\\\") — do not claim anything beyond the dispatched actions.\\"}","isError":false}]',NULL,'2026-10-25T23:35:18.897Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvogtxs3001bspwumew3m1gr','cb3d48a8-c2aa-4bb9-9f96-45bdd224be0a','user','Create 3 flashcards about anemia classification.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-25T23:35:21.411Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvogu3o0001kspwus6jn5ybc','cb3d48a8-c2aa-4bb9-9f96-45bdd224be0a','assistant','I''ll create 3 flashcards about anemia classification for you.

I''ve created 3 flashcards about anemia classification and added them to your review queue. The cards cover:

1. **Anemia classification by red blood cell morphology** - Microcytic, Normocytic, Macrocytic
2. **Common causes of microcytic anemia** - Iron deficiency, Thalassemia, Anemia of chronic disease, Sideroblastic anemia
3. **Classification by etiology (pathophysiologic)** - Production defects, Destruction defects, Blood loss

These cards are now due for immediate review (15 total cards due now) and will be resurfaced at expanding intervals as you rate your recall using the SM-2 spaced repetition system. You can access them through the Flashcards tab in your MedQ app.','[{"id":"call_-7142066516261857121","name":"create_flashcards","args":{"cards":[{"front":"Anemia classification by red blood cell morphology","back":"1. **Microcytic**: MCV < 80 fL (e.g., iron deficiency, thalassemia, anemia of chronic disease)\\n2. **Normocytic**: MCV 80-100 fL (e.g., anemia of chronic disease, hemolysis, early iron deficiency)\\n3. **Macrocytic**: MCV > 100 fL (e.g., folate/B12 deficiency, liver disease, hypothyroidism, alcoholism)","topic":"Hematology","system":"General"},{"front":"Common causes of microcytic anemia","back":"1. **Iron deficiency**: Most common cause worldwide\\n2. **Thalassemia**: Genetic defect in hemoglobin synthesis\\n3. **Anemia of chronic disease**: Functional iron deficiency due to inflammation\\n4. **Sideroblastic anemia**: Defective heme synthesis with ringed sideroblasts","topic":"Hematology","system":"General"},{"front":"Classification by etiology (pathophysiologic)","back":"1. **Production defects**: \\n   - Bone marrow failure (aplastic anemia)\\n   - Nutritional deficiencies (B12, folate, iron)\\n   - Chronic disease/inflammation\\n2. **Destruction defects**: \\n   - Hemolytic anemias (autoimmune, hereditary, acquired)\\n   - Mechanical destruction (e.g., DIC, TTP)\\n3. **Blood loss**: \\n   - Acute hemorrhage\\n   - Chronic blood loss","topic":"Hematology","system":"General"}],"deckLabel":"Anemia classification flashcards"}}]','[{"toolCallId":"call_-7142066516261857121","toolName":"create_flashcards","content":"{\\"created\\":true,\\"count\\":3,\\"cards\\":[{\\"id\\":\\"cmvogu1xc001espwur5pv7z54\\",\\"front\\":\\"Anemia classification by red blood cell morphology\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"cmvogu1xg001gspwuj0eu0fc3\\",\\"front\\":\\"Common causes of microcytic anemia\\"},{\\"id\\":\\"cmvogu1xi001ispwug1f28cqb\\",\\"front\\":\\"Classification by etiology (pathophysiologic)\\"}],\\"totalDueNow\\":15,\\"note\\":\\"Saved 3 flashcards to the learner''s review queue. Tell them the cards are due NOW (15 total due) on the Flashcards page, and SM-2 will resurface each card at expanding intervals as they rate their recall.\\"}","isError":false}]',NULL,'2026-10-25T23:35:29.040Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvogu5ls001nspwurzxw53zl','cb3d48a8-c2aa-4bb9-9f96-45bdd224be0a','user','Give me ONE USMLE-style clinical vignette question on sepsis. Do NOT reveal the answer yet — I want to attempt it first.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-25T23:35:31.552Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentThreadMessage" ("id","threadId","role","content","toolCalls","toolResults","metadata","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvoh0swu001sspwucaaybs6x','cb3d48a8-c2aa-4bb9-9f96-45bdd224be0a','assistant','I''ll create a USMLE-style clinical vignette question on sepsis for you.

I apologize, but the question generation tool timed out. Let me create a USMLE-style sepsis question directly for you instead:

**Clinical Vignette Question:**

A 68-year-old male with a history of type 2 diabetes mellitus and chronic kidney disease (baseline creatinine 1.8 mg/dL) presents to the emergency department with a 3-day history of worsening confusion, fever (39.2°C), and severe shortness of breath. His wife reports he has a non-healing ulcer on his right foot that has been increasing in size and producing foul-smelling discharge for the past week. On examination, he is tachycardic (heart rate 125 bpm), tachypneic (respiratory rate 28/min), and hypotensive (blood pressure 85/50 mmHg). His oxygen saturation is 88% on room air. Laboratory findings show:
- White blood cell count: 18,500/μL
- Lactate: 4.2 mmol/L
- Creatinine: 3.1 mg/dL (baseline 1.8 mg/dL)
- Glucose: 220 mg/dL
- Blood cultures: pending

Which of the following is the most appropriate initial management for this patient?

A. Administer intravenous ceftriaxone alone and observe for clinical improvement
B. Initiate intravenous fluids and broad-spectrum antibiotics, then reassess after 1 hour
C. Administer intravenous norepinephrine to maintain mean arterial pressure >65 mmHg
D. Start intravenous hydrocortisone 100 mg every 8 hours
E. Transfer to the intensive care unit for mechanical ventilation

