the cornerstone of RAAS inhibition for years and are key therapeutic options in patients with hypertension (HTN), ...\\n[S3] Angiotensin Receptor Blockers (ARBs)\\n    https://cvpharmacology.com/vasodilator/arb (cvpharmacology.com)\\n    Their mechanism of action, however, differs from ACE inhibitors , which inhibit the formation of angiotensin II. ARBs are receptor antagonists that block type 1 ... Read more","note":"Cite these inline as [S1], [S2]… markers placed right after the claim each source supports. NEVER paste raw URLs into the answer text — the interface renders [S#] markers as clickable source cards and lists every URL in a Web sources panel automatically. Results are re-ranked for recency (freshest first): when a source carries a date, mention the year the moment you cite it (e.g. \\"per the 2024 ESC guideline [S1]\\"), and prefer the most recent guidance when sources conflict — flag older sources as superseded where relevant."}',NULL,'2026-10-24T05:12:54.180Z');
