INSERT INTO "AgentToolExecution" ("id","userId","threadId","toolName","status","latencyMs","inputJson","outputJson","error","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvlyz115000fv6rdqy8f2wt6','cmusenqrl0000oir8zrgpm0p7','228c86f9-7798-44b5-b9cf-a72f67403045','search_medical_references','completed',1721,'{"query":"sepsis management guidelines Sepsis-3 bundle fluid resuscitation antibiotics","maxResults":4}','{"results":[{"title":"Evaluation and management of suspected sepsis and","url":"https://www.uptodate.com/contents/evaluation-and-management-of-suspected-sepsis-and-septic-shock-in-adults","snippet":"May 7, 2026 — Empiric antibiotic therapy is targeted at the suspected organism(s ) and site(s) of infection and preferably administered within the first hour. Read more","host":"www.uptodate.com","date":"May 7, 2026"},{"title":"Hospital Sepsis Program Core Elements","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/sepsis/hcp/core-elements/index.html","snippet":"Sep 21, 2026 — This document summarizes Core Elements of hospital sepsis programs, which are intended to monitor and optimize hospital management and outcomes ... Read more","host":"www.cdc.gov","date":"Sep 21, 2026"},{"title":"Surviving Sepsis Campaign Adult Guidelines","url":"https://sccm.org/survivingsepsiscampaign/guidelines-and-resources/surviving-sepsis-campaign-adult-guidelines","snippet":"For adults with probable or definite sepsis without shock, we “recommend” administering antimicrobial therapy immediately, ideally within 1 hr of recognition. Read more","host":"sccm.org","date":""},{"title":"Surviving sepsis campaign: international guidelines for  - PMC","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8486643","snippet":"by L Evans · 2021 · Cited by 10843 — The 2016 SSC guideline issued a recommendation for using a minimum of 30 ml/kg (ideal body weight) of IV crystalloids in initial fluid resuscitation . This fixed ... Read more","host":"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov","date":""}],"formatted":"[S1] Evaluation and management of suspected sepsis and (May 7, 2026)\\n    https://www.uptodate.com/contents/evaluation-and-management-of-suspected-sepsis-and-septic-shock-in-adults (www.uptodate.com)\\n    May 7, 2026 — Empiric antibiotic therapy is targeted at the suspected organism(s ) and site(s) of infection and preferably administered within the first hour. Read more\\n[S2] Hospital Sepsis Program Core Elements (Sep 21, 2026)\\n    https://www.cdc.gov/sepsis/hcp/core-elements/index.html (www.cdc.gov)\\n    Sep 21, 2026 — This document summarizes Core Elements of hospital sepsis programs, which are intended to monitor and optimize hospital management and outcomes ... Read more\\n[S3] Surviving Sepsis Campaign Adult Guidelines\\n    https://sccm.org/survivingsepsiscampaign/guidelines-and-resources/surviving-sepsis-campaign-adult-guidelines (sccm.org)\\n    For adults with probable or definite sepsis without shock, we “recommend” administering antimicrobial therapy immediately, ideally within 1 hr of recognition. Read more\\n[S4] Surviving sepsis campaign: international guidelines for  - PMC\\n    https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8486643 (pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov)\\n    by L Evans · 2021 · Cited by 10843 — The 2016 SSC guideline issued a recommendation for using a minimum of 30 ml/kg (ideal body weight) of IV crystalloids in initial fluid resuscitation . This fixed ... Read more","note":"Cite these inline as [S1], [S2]… markers placed right after the claim each source supports. NEVER paste raw URLs into the answer text — the interface renders [S#] markers as clickable source cards and lists every URL in a Web sources panel automatically. Results are re-ranked for recency (freshest first): when a source carries a date, mention the year the moment you cite it (e.g. \\"per the 2024 ESC guideline [S1]\\"), and prefer the most recent guidance when sources conflict — flag older sources as superseded where relevant."}',NULL,'2026-10-24T05:39:53.465Z');
