t in the cells.\\n[S3] Becker muscular dystrophy caused by an intronic mutation\\n    https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0960896608006822 (www.sciencedirect.com)\\n    by B Baskin · 2009 · Cited by 15 — Mutations in the dystrophin (DMD) gene can cause both the severe Duchenne MD (DMD) and the milder Becker MD (BMD) phenotype. In the majority of boys with DMD, ... Read more","note":"Cite these inline as [S1], [S2]… markers placed right after the claim each source supports. NEVER paste raw URLs into the answer text — the interface renders [S#] markers as clickable source cards and lists every URL in a Web sources panel automatically. Results are re-ranked for recency (freshest first): when a source carries a date, mention the year the moment you cite it (e.g. \\"per the 2024 ESC guideline [S1]\\"), and prefer the most recent guidance when sources conflict — flag older sources as superseded where relevant."}',NULL,'2026-10-24T13:24:17.223Z');
