INSERT INTO "AgentToolExecution" ("id","userId","threadId","toolName","status","latencyMs","inputJson","outputJson","error","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvlzks36001uv6rdqggqkk0t','cmusenr950006oir80jr4ludo',NULL,'save_question','completed',10396,'{"type":"mcq","text":"A 6-year-old child presents with constipation that began at age 3 years. The child has hard stools, straining during defecation, and stools less than 3 times per week for the past 2 months. Physical examination is normal. What is the most appropriate diagnosis and what key diagnostic criteria must be met?","options":["Organic constipation - requires evidence of structural abnormality on imaging","Functional constipation - must meet Rome IV criteria of 2+ symptoms occurring at least once weekly for 1 month","Functional constipation - requires abdominal distension and palpable fecal mass","Organic constipation - requires family history of Hirschsprung disease"],"answer":"Functional constipation - must meet Rome IV criteria of 2+ symptoms occurring at least once weekly for 1 month","explanation":"Functional constipation is a clinical diagnosis based on history and physical examination, with no evidence of organic disease. The Rome IV criteria require at least 2 of the following occurring at least once weekly for 1 month: 2 or fewer defecations per week, retentive posturing, painful or hard bowel movements, large fecal mass in rectum, or fecal incontinence [S1]. This child meets criteria with hard stools, straining, and decreased frequency.","mnemonic":"ROME criteria: 2+ symptoms, weekly, monthly duration","clinicalPearl":"Functional constipation is diagnosed clinically using Rome IV criteria; organic causes are rare (<5% of cases) and require red flag evaluation [S5].","distractorAnalysis":"Option A is incorrect because organic constipation requires specific structural/organic findings, not just symptoms. Option C is incorrect because abdominal distension and fecal mass are supportive but not diagnostic criteria. Option D is incorrect because family history is a red flag but not diagnostic criteria.","difficulty":"Medium","system":"Gastrointestinal","topic":"Constipation diagnosis","tags":["functional constipation","Rome criteria","diagnosis"],"imageUrl":"","audioUrl":"","illustrationDescription":"","attachSourceMediaId":"","citations":[{"sourceId":"cmv6xgvop0000xurml1w3mzsy","chunkId":"cmv6yxa2b004xi8rml3uq311z"},{"sourceId":"cmv6xgvop0000xurml1w3mzsy","chunkId":"cmv6yxa2b0059i8rmv0gfj0f7"},{"sourceId":"cmv6xgvop0000xurml1w3mzsy","chunkId":"cmv6yxa2b005ki8rmgwfl542w"}]}','{"saved":true,"id":"cmvlzl03u001vv6rd2yxtqoyr","index":1,"citations":1,"message":"Question 1 saved (id cmvlzl03u001vv6rd2yxtqoyr), 1 citation. Continue with the next question or summarize when done."}',NULL,'2026-10-24T05:56:48.306Z');
