INSERT INTO "AgentToolExecution" ("id","userId","threadId","toolName","status","latencyMs","inputJson","outputJson","error","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvm0lcxe001fwnrdayy56oc4','cmuser2vb0000scr8wuwwi596','0393944e-1fd0-4325-bffc-420f132f5106','save_question','completed',300005,'{"type":"mcq","text":"A 45-year-old female presents with fatigue, pallor, and shortness of breath. Her laboratory results show: Hemoglobin 7.8 g/dL, MCV 78 fL, MCH 26 pg, MCHC 33 g/dL, RDW 18%. Peripheral smear shows microcytic hypochromic red blood cells. What is the most likely underlying cause of her anemia?","options":["Iron deficiency anemia","Vitamin B12 deficiency","Folate deficiency","Anemia of chronic disease","Hemolytic anemia"],"answer":"Iron deficiency anemia","explanation":"The patient''s presentation with fatigue, pallor, and shortness of breath along with laboratory findings of microcytic (low MCV) hypochromic (low MCHC) anemia with elevated RDW is classic for iron deficiency anemia. The RDW is elevated due to anisocytosis (variation in red blood cell size), which is common in iron deficiency as red blood cells become progressively smaller. Iron deficiency is the most common cause of anemia worldwide and should be suspected in patients with these findings.","mnemonic":"\\"Microcytic hypochromic with high RDW = iron deficiency\\"","clinicalPearl":"Iron deficiency anemia is the most common nutritional deficiency worldwide and the most common cause of anemia overall.","distractorAnalysis":"Vitamin B12 and folate deficiencies typically cause macrocytic anemia (high MCV), not microcytic. Anemia of chronic disease usually shows normal or high MCV and normal RDW. Hemolytic anemia typically shows normocytic cells and reticulocytosis.","difficulty":"Medium","system":"General","topic":"anemia","tags":["hematology","iron deficiency","microcytic anemia"],"imageUrl":"","audioUrl":"","illustrationDescription":"Blood smear showing microcytic hypochromic red blood cells characteristic of iron deficiency anemia"}','{"approved":false,"reason":"Timed out waiting for approval (5 minutes).","note":"Do not retry this tool call in this turn. Acknowledge the decision to the user and continue without performing the action."}',NULL,'2026-10-24T06:25:14.931Z');
