ished intervals differ from it materially — mostly by sitting lower, a range of 3 to ...\\n[S3] Biochemistry, Anion Gap - StatPearls - NCBI Bookshelf\\n    https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK539757 (www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov)\\n    by DG Pandey · 2023 · Cited by 16 — a normal anion gap depends on the concentration of phosphate and albumin in the serum and ranges from 4 to 12 mmol/L. 4 to 12 mmol/L range is for “ normal anion ...","note":"Cite these inline as [S1], [S2]… markers placed right after the claim each source supports. NEVER paste raw URLs into the answer text — the interface renders [S#] markers as clickable source cards and lists every URL in a Web sources panel automatically. Results are re-ranked for recency (freshest first): when a source carries a date, mention the year the moment you cite it (e.g. \\"per the 2024 ESC guideline [S1]\\"), and prefer the most recent guidance when sources conflict — flag older sources as superseded where relevant."}',NULL,'2026-10-24T10:42:39.159Z');
