odalities. The blood pressure discrepancy between arms is a classic finding supporting aortic dissection, and CT angiography remains the preferred initial diagnostic test.","mnemonic":"CTA: Gold standard for dissection (high sensitivity/specificity)","clinicalPearl":"Blood pressure discrepancy between arms is a classic sign of aortic dissection and should prompt urgent imaging.","distractorAnalysis":"TEE: High sensitivity but less accessible than CTA; MRI: Excellent but less available; D-dimer: Poor sensitivity in acute dissection; TTE: Lower sensitivity than other modalities","difficulty":"Hard","system":"Cardiovascular","topic":"aortic dissection diagnosis","tags":["diagnostic imaging","emergency medicine","cardiovascular"],"imageUrl":"","audioUrl":"","illustrationDescription":"CT angiography image showing aortic dissection"}','{"approved":false,"reason":"The request was cancelled.","note":"Do not retry this tool call in this turn. Acknowledge the decision to the user and continue without performing the action."}',NULL,'2026-10-24T08:18:58.039Z');
