ih.gov/books/NBK470284 (www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov)\\n    by LV Simon · 2025 · Cited by 131 — Clinical manifestations generally appear at levels above 6.0 mEq/L. However, the rate of change exerts greater influence than absolute values . Read more\\n[S3] Management of Hyperkalaemia in Adults – October 2023\\n    https://www.ukkidney.org/sites/default/files/FINAL%20VERSION%20-%20UKKA%20CLINICAL%20PRACTICE%20GUIDELINE%20-%20MANAGEMENT%20OF%20HYPERKALAEMIA%20IN%20ADULTS%20-%20191223_0.pdf (www.ukkidney.org)\\n    by A Alfonzo · Cited by 121 — Give 30ml over 10 min. Hyperkalaemia is a medical disorder in which the potassium (K+) level in the blood is raised. this guideline provides guidance for ...","note":"Cite these inline as [S1], [S2]… markers placed right after the claim each source supports. NEVER paste raw URLs into the answer text — the interface renders [S#] markers as clickable source cards and lists every URL in a Web sources panel automatically. Results are re-ranked for recency (freshest first): when a source carries a date, mention the year the moment you cite it (e.g. \\"per the 2024 ESC guideline [S1]\\"), and prefer the most recent guidance when sources conflict — flag older sources as superseded where relevant."}',NULL,'2026-10-24T08:41:07.543Z');
