 there anything else I need to know about a potassium blood ... Read more\\n[S3] Serum Potassium - Clinical Methods - NCBI Bookshelf - NIH\\n    https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK307 (www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov)\\n    by A Rastegar · 1990 · Cited by 99 — Normal serum potassium is 3.5 to 5.5 mEq/L ; however, plasma potassium is 0.5 mEq/L lower. While total body potassium is lower in females and in older patients, ... Read more","note":"Cite these inline as [S1], [S2]… markers placed right after the claim each source supports. NEVER paste raw URLs into the answer text — the interface renders [S#] markers as clickable source cards and lists every URL in a Web sources panel automatically. Results are re-ranked for recency (freshest first): when a source carries a date, mention the year the moment you cite it (e.g. \\"per the 2024 ESC guideline [S1]\\"), and prefer the most recent guidance when sources conflict — flag older sources as superseded where relevant."}',NULL,'2026-10-24T08:41:10.296Z');
