P waves. S complexes usually < 120ms, Irregularly irregular ventricular rate\\n[S3] Atrial Fibrillation: Knowing the Basics\\n    https://clinicalview.gehealthcare.com/white-paper/atrial-fibrillation-knowing-basics (clinicalview.gehealthcare.com)\\n    by ECG General — ECG showing atrial fibrillation Atrial fibrillation: “irregularly irregular” ventricular rhythm with an absence of P waves and often irregular waves in the ... Read more","note":"Cite these inline as [S1], [S2]… markers placed right after the claim each source supports. NEVER paste raw URLs into the answer text — the interface renders [S#] markers as clickable source cards and lists every URL in a Web sources panel automatically. Results are re-ranked for recency (freshest first): when a source carries a date, mention the year the moment you cite it (e.g. \\"per the 2024 ESC guideline [S1]\\"), and prefer the most recent guidance when sources conflict — flag older sources as superseded where relevant."}',NULL,'2026-10-24T17:27:57.308Z');
