INSERT INTO "AgentToolExecution" ("id","userId","threadId","toolName","status","latencyMs","inputJson","outputJson","error","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvmwypb30019g7rdyxfl9yu9','cmusenqrl0000oir8zrgpm0p7',NULL,'save_question','completed',2631,'{"type":"mcq","text":"A 72-year-old nursing home resident with chronic constipation is started on a medication that increases water content in the stool and stimulates peristalsis. Which of the following pharmacological agents was most likely prescribed?","options":["Polyethylene glycol","Bisacodyl","Docusate sodium","Loperamide","Methylnaltrexone"],"answer":"Polyethylene glycol","explanation":"Polyethylene glycol (PEG) is an osmotic laxative that works by retaining water in the colon, increasing stool water content and softening stool consistency [S1]. It also has a mild stimulatory effect on peristalsis due to increased stool volume [S1]. PEG is considered first-line therapy for chronic constipation in older adults due to its efficacy and safety profile.","mnemonic":"PEG = Pumps water into stool = Easier elimination = Gentle (PEG)","clinicalPearl":"Polyethylene glycol is often preferred over stimulant laxatives for chronic constipation in elderly patients because it doesn''t cause dependency or electrolyte disturbances with long-term use. The typical dose is 17-34 grams daily, with effects seen within 24-48 hours.","distractorAnalysis":"Option B (bisacodyl) is a stimulant laxative that directly stimulates colonic nerves, not primarily through osmotic effects. Option C (docusate) is a stool softener that decreases surface tension but has minimal effect on peristalsis. Option D (loperamide) is an anti-diarrheal agent that inhibits peristalsis. Option E (methylnaltrexone) is used for opioid-induced constipation and works by blocking mu-opioid receptors.","difficulty":"Medium","system":"pharmacology","topic":"Constipation","tags":["gastrointestinal","laxatives","geriatrics"],"imageUrl":"","audioUrl":"","illustrationDescription":"","attachSourceMediaId":"","citations":[{"sourceId":"cmuyzuuww0002ewma8ndzgi1c","chunkId":"cmuyzuwto0004ewmapgbod3b9"},{"sourceId":"cmuyygery0003ydma3bobkh6a","chunkId":"cmuyygrw90009ydmarc4okdbf"}]}','{"saved":true,"id":"cmvmwyrc4001ag7rdk3orcxfk","index":2,"message":"Question 2 saved (id cmvmwyrc4001ag7rdk3orcxfk). Continue with the next question or summarize when done."}',NULL,'2026-10-24T21:31:25.215Z');
