mcq","system":"Pharmacology","topic":"Nitrates","difficulty":"Medium","preview":"A 67-year-old patient with stable angina pectoris is prescribed sublingual nitroglycerin for acute episodes. Which of the following statemen"},{"index":6,"id":"cmvmww2nc000lg7rdzl3dbt2h","type":"mcq","system":"Pharmacology","topic":"Antiarrhythmics","difficulty":"Medium","preview":"A 72-year-old patient with atrial fibrillation and a rapid ventricular response is started on flecainide. According to the Vaughan-Williams "},{"index":7,"id":"cmvmwwea8000ng7rdediqakvg","type":"mcq","system":"Pharmacology","topic":"Statins","difficulty":"Medium","preview":"A 62-year-old patient with hyperlipidemia and established coronary artery disease has an LDL cholesterol level of 130 mg/dL despite lifestyl"},{"index":8,"id":"cmvmwwqk3000pg7rdrzwanpgp","type":"mcq","system":"Pharmacology","topic":"ACE inhibitors/ARBs","difficulty":"Medium","preview":"A 55-year-old patient with hypertension and chronic kidney stage 3 disease (eGFR 45 mL/min) is being evaluated for antihypertensive therapy."}],"note":"The generation agent reported an error — apologize and suggest retrying. Never fabricate saved questions."}',NULL,'2026-10-24T21:24:04.639Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentToolExecution" ("id","userId","threadId","toolName","status","latencyMs","inputJson","outputJson","error","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvmwxv98000yg7rdkca2j3mc','cmuser2vb0000scr8wuwwi596',NULL,'save_question','completed',9162,'{"type":"mcq","text":"A 68-year-old patient with congestive heart failure (HFrEF) and hypertension presents to clinic. Current medications include furosemide, lisinopril, and carvedilol. Which of the following calcium channel blockers would be most appropriate to add for blood pressure control in this patient?","options":["Amlodipine","Diltiazem","Verapamil","Nifedipine","Isradipine"],"answer":"Amlodipine","explanation":"Amlodipine, a dihydropyridine calcium channel blocker, is the most appropriate choice for this patient with HFrEF. Non-dihydropyridine calcium channel blockers (diltiazem and verapamil) are contraindicated in heart failure with reduced ejection fraction due to their negative inotropic effects, which can worsen cardiac function [S2]. Nifedipine and isradipine, while dihydropyridines, are less commonly used first-line compared to amlodipine due to reflex tachycardia and other adverse effects. Amlodipine has been shown to be safe and effective in heart failure patients and does not worsen outcomes [S1].","mnemonic":"Dihydropyridines = Safe in HFrEF (Diltiazem/Verapamil = Don''t use)","clinicalPearl":"Non-dihydropyridine calcium channel blockers (verapamil, diltiazem) are contraindicated in HFrEF due to negative inotropic effects, while dihydropyridines (amlodipine) are generally safe.","distractorAnalysis":"Diltiazem and Verapamil are incorrect as they are non-dihydropyridines that worsen heart failure. Nifedipine and isradipine are dihydropyridines but are not first-line choices due to adverse effects like reflex tachycardia.","difficulty":"Medium","system":"cardiovascular","topic":"calcium channel blockers","tags":["heart failure","hypertension","calcium channel blockers","pharmacology"],"imageUrl":"","audioUrl":"","illustrationDescription":"","attachSourceMediaId":"","citations":[{"sourceId":"cmv6wresk0012j6rmn8yzcdiz","chunkId":"cmv6ytwoh001tbjrm7m3ub6ju"},{"sourceId":"cmv6wresk0012j6rmn8yzcdiz","chunkId":"cmv6ytwol00fwbjrmry1ogjnh"}]}','{"saved":true,"id":"cmvmwy2bl000zg7rdss1e0kvy","index":1,"message":"Question 1 saved (id cmvmwy2bl000zg7rdss1e0kvy). Continue with the next question or summarize when done."}',NULL,'2026-10-24T21:30:46.268Z');
INSERT INTO "AgentToolExecution" ("id","userId","threadId","toolName","status","latencyMs","inputJson","outputJson","error","createdAt") VALUES ('cmvmwy8ot0010g7rdpd2ritse','cmuser2vb0000scr8wuwwi596',NULL,'save_question','completed',9065,'{"type":"mcq","text":"A 52-year-old male with hyperlipidemia is started on simvastatin 40mg daily. Two months later, he presents with severe muscle pain and weakness. Laboratory tests show creatine kinase (CK) elevated to 10 times the upper limit of normal. Which of the following statements regarding this patient''s condition is most accurate?","options":["Simvastatin has the lowest risk of rhabdomyolysis among all statins","The risk of rhabdomyolysis is independent of statin dose","Concurrent use of cytochrome P450 inhibitors would increase the risk","Rhabdomyolysis typically occurs within the first week of statin therapy","CK elevation is not a reliable indicator of muscle injury"],"answer":"Concurrent use of cytochrome P450 inhibitors would increase the risk","explanation":"The patient''s presentation is consistent with statin-induced rhabdomyolysis. Simvastatin actually has one of the highest risks of rhabdomyolysis among statins, with studies showing it has more than a 2-fold increased likelihood compared to other statins [S3]. The risk of rhabdomyolysis increases with higher statin doses [S1]. Concurrent use of cytochrome P450 inhibitors (such as clarithromycin, cyclosporine, and grapefruit juice) significantly increases the risk by reducing statin metabolism and increasing systemic exposure [S2]. Rhabdomyolysis typically occurs after weeks to months of therapy, not within the first week, and CK elevation is a reliable indicator of muscle injury [S1].","mnemonic":"Simvastatin + CYP inhibitors = High risk rhabdomyolysis","clinicalPearl":"Simvastatin carries higher rhabdomyolysis risk than other statins, and this risk is significantly increased when combined with CYP450 inhibitors.","distractorAnalysis":"Option A is incorrect as simvastatin has higher risk. Option B is wrong as risk increases with dose. Option D is incorrect as rhabdomyolysis typically occurs after weeks. Option E is wrong as CK is a reliable indicator.","difficulty":"Medium","system":"cardiovascular","topic":"statins","tags":["hyperlipidemia","statins","rhabdomyolysis","drug interactions"],"imageUrl":"","audioUrl":"","illustrationDescription":"","attachSourceMediaId":"","citations":[{"sourceId":"cmv6wresk0012j6rmn8yzcdiz","chunkId":"cmv6ytwoh001tbjrm7m3ub6ju"},{"sourceId":"cmv6wresk0012j6rmn8yzcdiz","chunkId":"cmv6ytwol00fwbjrmry1ogjnh"}]}','{"saved":true,"id":"cmvmwyfoj0011g7rdcqqlhbof","index":2,"message":"Question 2 saved (id cmvmwyfoj0011g7rdcqqlhbof). Continue with the next question or summarize when done."}',NULL,'2026-10-24T21:31:03.677Z');
